{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\n\nImplement 10 SOS (Magic: The Gathering set) card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`:\n- **SOS 1** — The Dawning Archaic: `{10}` Legendary Creature — Avatar, 7/7. \"This spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard. Reach. Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n- **SOS 4** — Together as One: `{6}` Sorcery. \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\"\n- **SOS 13** — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares: `{1}{W}{W} // {W}` Creature — Cat Cleric // Instant, 3/3. \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared. (While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.)\" Keyword: Prepared.\n- **SOS 57** — Mana Sculpt: `{1}{U}{U}` Instant. \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n- **SOS 97** — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer: `{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, loyalty 3. \"+1: Surveil 2. −1: Any number of target players each discard a card. −2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is the number of coins that came up heads.\"\n- **SOS 120** — Improvisation Capstone: `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson. \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana costs. Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\"\n- **SOS 201** — Lorehold, the Historian: `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5. \"Flying, haste. Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. (You may cast a card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.) At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\"\n- **SOS 226** — Silverquill, the Disputant: `{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4. \"Flying, vigilance. Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.)\"\n- **SOS 245** — Witherbloom, the Balancer: `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5. \"Affinity for creatures (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control.). Flying, deathtouch. Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n- **SOS 257** — Great Hall of the Biblioplex: Land. \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell. {5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n\nEach `card_impl.py` class name is predetermined (TheDawningArchaic, TogetherAsOne, EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares, ManaSculpt, RalZarekGuestLecturer, ImprovisationCapstone, LoreholdTheHistorian, SilverquillTheDisputant, WitherbloomTheBalancer, GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex).\n\nThe user is expected to make engine changes to implement new keywords/mechanics, and should write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n- MTG rules engine in pure Python (stdlib only). Imported as `engine`.\n- CardImpl hook methods: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`, `on_cast`, `on_resolve`, `get_targets`, `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`, `get_loyalty_abilities` (Planeswalker), `get_mana_abilities` (Land/permanents).\n- Triggered abilities via `TriggerManager.register(TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller))`; events are typed dataclasses (subclass matching). APNAP ordering.\n- Replacement effects via `ReplacementManager.register(ReplacementEffect(event_type, source, condition, replacement, controller))`; \"instead\" semantics, `event.prevented`/`event.destination`.\n- Continuous effects via `EffectManager.add(ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, duration))`; 7-layer system; DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0, DURATION_PERMANENT=-1.\n- Mana: `ManaPool` with `last_payment_colors` for Converge; `card.colors_spent` set by cast_spell after payment.\n- Cost reduction: `cost_reduction(game)` returns generic reduction, clamped to not go below 0 generic; only reduces generic.\n- Casting: `cast_spell()` and `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` (free cast from any zone, e.g. graveyard/exile).\n- Mechanics needed: Converge, cost reduction (Affinity), counterspell, planeswalker loyalty abilities, attack triggers, upkeep triggers, surveil, miracle, casualty, paradigm, prepared/MDFC, lands becoming creatures, coin flips, extra turns/skip turns.\n- `game.extra_turns: list[int]` FIFO queue for extra turns; `_normal_next_index` tracking.\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections\n\n- **engine/card.py**: Class hierarchy. `CardImpl.__init__(name, mana_cost, card_types, subtypes, supertypes, keywords, rules_text, owner, controller)`. `_reset_characteristics()` resets card_types/keywords (Creature also resets P/T and counters and `protections=[]`). `Creature` has base_power/base_toughness, modified_power/modified_toughness, plus_one_counters, `power`/`toughness` properties, `_base_plus_one_counters`. `Planeswalker(starting_loyalty)` has `loyalty`, `get_loyalty_abilities()`. `Land` has `can_cast()->False`, `get_mana_abilities()`. `Instant`/`Sorcery`/`Enchantment`/`Aura`/`Artifact`/`ArtifactCreature`. Dataclasses: `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)`, `ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description)`, `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`, `Mode(name, description)`, `ContinuousEffect`.\n\n- **engine/events.py**: Typed events. Triggered: EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent, controller, card, creature), LeavesBattlefieldTriggeredEvent, DealsDamageTriggeredEvent(source, target, amount, is_combat, combat), DrawsCardTriggeredEvent, BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent, EndStepTriggeredEvent(player), CreatureDiesTriggeredEvent, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller), AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker), GainsLifeTriggeredEvent, LosesLifeTriggeredEvent, CounterAddedTriggeredEvent. Replacement: MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination, controller, owner, prevented; `.card` property), CreatureDiesReplacementEvent(creature), PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent(permanent), SacrificeReplacementEvent(permanent), CreateTokenReplacementEvent, AddCounterReplacementEvent.\n\n- **engine/triggers.py**: `TriggerManager.register/unregister(source)/fire_event(game, event)`. fire_event matches by isinstance (subclass match), checks condition(game, event), pushes StackObject(source, controller, on_resolve=trigger.effect) in APNAP order.\n\n- **engine/casting.py**: `cast_spell(game, player, card)` — timing, can_cast, hand check, hand→stack, choose targets (validates filter_fn, protection), cost reduction, pay mana, sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`, on_cast, push StackObject with `_on_resolve` → `_resolve_spell`. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` — no timing/mana. `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets`, calls on_resolve, moves permanent→battlefield or non-permanent→graveyard via move_to_zone. **IMPORTANT: cast_spell does NOT fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent.**\n\n- **engine/zones.py**: `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None)` — handles replacement redirection (only when leaving battlefield), fires LeavesBattlefield/CreatureDies, registers/unregisters triggers+replacements, fires EntersBattlefield. `move_zone()` lower-level; deletes `colors_spent` on zone change.\n\n- **engine/game.py**: Helpers: `deal_damage`, `destroy`, `sacrifice`, `exile`, `draw_card` (tracks `cards_drawn_this_turn`), `discard`, `create_token` (fires ETB, registers triggers/replacements), `add_counter(game, permanent, counter_type, amount)` (supports \"+1/+1\", \"-1/-1\", \"loyalty\", generic), `remove_counter`, `tap`, `untap`. `run_game`, `_check_game_over`.\n\n- **engine/game_state.py**: `GameState` with active_player/non_active_player/priority_player properties, get_battlefield/hand/graveyard/library/exile, `advance_phase()`, `_TURN_SEQUENCE`, `extra_turns`, `empty_mana_pools`.\n\n- **engine/stack.py**: `StackObject(source, controller, targets, on_resolve, is_mana_ability)`. `Stack` (push/pop/peek/objects). `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` — for spell copies (casualty). `priority_loop`, `resolve_top`.\n\n- **engine/abilities.py**: `activate_ability(game, player, ability)` dispatches to LoyaltyAbilityInstance or ActivatedAbilityInstance. `tap_cost(game, source)`. Loyalty: sorcery-speed only, once-per-turn (`_loyalty_activated_this_turn` set, `clear_loyalty_tracking()`), adjusts loyalty. `ActivatedAbilityInstance(source, controller, cost, effect, is_mana_ability, description)`, `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source, controller, loyalty_cost, effect, description)`.\n\n- **engine/turn.py**: `run_turn`, `_do_untap_step`, `_do_draw_step` (starting player skips turn-1 draw), `_do_combat_step`, `_do_cleanup_step`. Upkeep fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()`. **No EndStepTriggeredEvent fired.** `_NO_PRIORITY_STEPS` = untap+cleanup.\n\n- **engine/combat.py**: `declare_attackers_step` taps attackers (unless vigilance), sets is_attacking. **Does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent.** `_can_attack`, `_can_block`, `_get_lethal_damage`, `_deal_damage`, `combat_damage_step`.\n\n- **engine/continuous_effects.py**: Layer (1-7), SubLayer (7a-7d), EffectManager.add/remove/remove_expired/apply_all (resets battlefield objects then reapplies).\n\n- **engine/mana.py**: ManaPool.add/empty/total/get/can_pay/pay; `last_payment_colors`; hybrid backtracking.\n\n- **engine/types.py**: Enums Color, ManaType(incl COLORLESS), Zone, Phase, Step, CardType, Supertype(BASIC/LEGENDARY/SNOW), Keyword(Flag: FLYING, FIRST_STRIKE, DOUBLE_STRIKE, DEATHTOUCH, TRAMPLE, LIFELINK, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE, FLASH, DEFENDER, HEXPROOF, INDESTRUCTIBLE, MENACE, WARD, PROWESS). `ManaCost(generic, pips, x_count, hybrid)` with `.cmc` and `.parse()`. `HybridManaSymbol`. `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)`.\n\n- **test_utils.py**: `create_game(deck1, deck2, *, scripts=...)`, `set_board_state(game, player_index, *, battlefield, hand, graveyard, life, mana)`, `cast_spell(game, player_index, card_name, targets=None)` (scripts targets into player via `player._script.appendleft`), `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers(game, attacker_names)`, `declare_blockers(game, assignments)`, `card_colors(card)`. `_resolve_top_of_stack` pops+resolves.\n\n- **FDN reference patterns** (read fdn_13, fdn_142, fdn_205, fdn_215, fdn_244, fdn_81, fdn_44, fdn_48, fdn_153, fdn_245, fdn_254):\n  - **fdn_205 (Converge)**: stores `self.colors_spent` (int default 0), on_resolve reads it for token count. NOTE: engine sets `card.colors_spent = list(...colors)` (a LIST), but this card uses int — tests set it directly.\n  - **fdn_244 (Progenitus/replacement)**: `register_replacement_effects` registers `ReplacementEffect(event_type=MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent, source=self, condition=lambda g,e: e.card is source, replacement=..., controller=...)`. Protection via `self.protections = [ProtectionAbility(quality='everything', predicate=lambda s: True)]`, re-applied in overridden `_reset_characteristics`.\n  - **fdn_48/fdn_153 (counterspell)**: `_get_chosen_target(card, game)` reads `chosen_targets[0]` or `_resolve_target`. `_counter_spell(game, stack_obj)` removes from `game.stack._items`, removes card from controller's STACK zone, adds to owner's graveyard. `can_cast` checks stack for valid spell; `get_targets` returns TargetRequirement with zone=Zone.STACK targeting StackObjects.\n  - **fdn_81/fdn_44 (planeswalker)**: `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns `[LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description), ...]`. Effects read `pw._resolve_target`/`_resolve_targets`/`_damage_assignments` (set externally by tests). `register_triggers` for passive abilities. Uses TriggerRegistration with event conditions reading `event.creature`, `event.source`, `event.combat`.\n  - **fdn_245/fdn_254 (mana abilities)**: `get_mana_abilities()` returns `[ManaAbility(cost=_tap_cost, mana_produced=_effect, description=...)]` where `_effect(game)` does `controller.mana_pool.add(mtype, 1)`. `_tap_cost(game, source)` checks/sets is_tapped.\n  - **fdn_215 (modal)**: `get_modes()` returns `[Mode(...), ...]`; `self.chosen_mode` int dispatches in on_resolve.\n  - **fdn_13**: targeted instant pattern with `_is_on_battlefield`, add_counter then sync `_base_plus_one_counters`, continuous effect for flying until EOT.\n  - **fdn_142**: `make_vanilla(\"Healer's Hawk\", \"{W}\", 1, 1, keywords=..., creature_types={\"Bird\"})` for simple keyword creatures.\n\n## 4. Errors and Fixes\nNone yet — still in research phase, no code written or executed.\n\n## 5. Problem Solving\n- Discovered that `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, and `EndStepTriggeredEvent` are defined but never fired by the engine. These will need to be wired up (in cast_spell, declare_attackers_step, and the END step respectively) to support SOS 1 (attack trigger), SOS 201/226/257 (cast triggers), and any end-step needs — while being careful not to break existing engine_tests (especially test_casting.py which has strict assertions about cast_spell behavior).\n- Confirmed engine modifications must be additive-only (no rename/move/delete of existing engine items).\n- Confirmed grading uses authoritative test copies; my tests are for local verification only.\n\n## 6. All User Messages\n1. (System reminders about deferred tools via ToolSearch and available skills.)\n2. \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly — they have rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`. You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n3. \"Tool loaded.\" (after ToolSearch loaded TaskCreate/TaskUpdate/TaskList)\n4. (Final message) Instruction to produce this