ementation or engine modification — all 10 `card_impl.py` files still contain only the `pass` stub. No tests run yet.\n\n## 9. Optional Next Step\nBegin implementing the engine changes and the simpler cards. The natural next step, directly in line with the task, is to start with engine event-firing wiring (fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` at the end of `cast_spell`/`cast_spell_free`, `AttacksTriggeredEvent` in `declare_attackers_step`, and `EndStepTriggeredEvent` in the END step of `run_turn`), then implement the cards starting with the straightforward ones (SOS 245 Witherbloom — Affinity/cost_reduction + keywords; SOS 226 Silverquill — casualty; SOS 4 Together as One — Converge; SOS 57 Mana Sculpt — counterspell). Per the task: \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics\" and \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257.\" I should verify each engine change against `engine_tests/` by running `pytest` and write per-card tests under `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/f8a3aed6-12f8-4341-9631-2336f98abe5d.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8a3aed6-12f8-4341-9631-2336f98abe5d","uuid":"193dd17d-74b1-4faa-b8f9-5262486dbf76","timestamp":"2026-06-04T05:47:02.785Z","isSynthetic":true}
