{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (Magic: The Gathering set) card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`, filling in the `card_impl.py` template (currently `pass` stubs) for each. The class names are predetermined and must remain in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`:\n   - **SOS 1 — TheDawningArchaic** (Creature, subtypes {'Avatar'}, LEGENDARY, 7/7, `{10}`): \"This spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard. Reach. Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n   - **SOS 4 — TogetherAsOne** (Sorcery, `{6}`, Converge): \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\"\n   - **SOS 13 — EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares** (Creature, subtypes {Cat, Cleric}, LEGENDARY, 3/3, `{1}{W}{W} // {W}`, Prepared): ETB target player creates a 1/1 white-black Inkling flying token; then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared. While prepared, may cast a copy of its spell (Swords to Plowshares — Exile target creature, controller gains life = its power); doing so unprepares it.\n   - **SOS 57 — ManaSculpt** (Instant, `{1}{U}{U}`): \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n   - **SOS 97 — RalZarekGuestLecturer** (Planeswalker, subtypes {'Ral'}, LEGENDARY, loyalty 3, `{1}{B}{B}`): +1 Surveil 2; −1 any number of target players each discard a card; −2 return target creature card MV≤3 from your graveyard to battlefield; −7 flip five coins, target opponent skips next X turns (X = heads).\n   - **SOS 120 — ImprovisationCapstone** (Sorcery — Lesson, `{5}{R}{R}`, Paradigm): Exile from top of library until total MV ≥ 4; cast any number for free. Paradigm.\n   - **SOS 201 — LoreholdTheHistorian** (Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, `{3}{R}{W}`): Flying, haste; each instant/sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}; at beginning of each opponent's upkeep, may discard a card to draw a card.\n   - **SOS 226 — SilverquillTheDisputant** (Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4, `{2}{W}{B}`): Flying, vigilance; each instant/sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1.\n   - **SOS 245 — WitherbloomTheBalancer** (Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, `{6}{B}{G}`): Affinity for creatures (self); Flying, deathtouch; instant/sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\n   - **SOS 257 — GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex** (Land): {T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color (spend only on instant/sorcery). {5}: becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn\"; still a land.\n   \n   The user expects engine changes to implement new keywords/mechanics, and to write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (max 30 tests per card).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pure-Python (stdlib only) MTG rules engine, imported as `engine`. Bare package imports from workspace root.\n   - CardImpl hooks: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)->int` (generic reduction only, clamped ≥0), `on_cast`, `on_resolve`, `get_targets`, `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`, plus subclass-specific `get_loyalty_abilities` (Planeswalker), `get_mana_abilities` (Land).\n   - Triggered abilities: `TriggerManager.register(TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller))`; `fire_event(game, event)` matches by isinstance (subclass-aware), checks condition, pushes StackObject in APNAP order.\n   - Replacement effects: `ReplacementManager.register(ReplacementEffect(event_type, source, condition, replacement, controller))`; `apply()` returns possibly-mutated event; \"instead\" semantics; only consulted on battlefield-leave moves in `move_to_zone`.\n   - Continuous effects: `EffectManager.add(ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration))`; 7-layer system; `DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0`, `DURATION_PERMANENT=-1`; `apply_all` resets battlefield via `_reset_characteristics()` then reapplies.\n   - Mana: `ManaPool.last_payment_colors` (list of distinct Colors, colorless excluded, sorted). `cast_spell` sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`. Converge color count = `len(set(colors_spent))`.\n   - `cast_spell(game, player, card)` and `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` (no timing/mana, casts from any zone like graveyard/exile).\n   - `game.extra_turns: list[int]` FIFO of seat indices — append a player's index to grant them an inserted extra turn.\n   - DeterministicPlayer pops scripted answers via `choose`/`choose_target`/`choose_yes_no`/`choose_card`/`assign_damage_order`.\n   - Surveil implemented inline (no engine helper) using `controller.choose_yes_no` per top card.\n   - test_utils: `create_game`, `set_board_state`, `cast_spell` (scripts targets via `player._script.appendleft`), `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers`, `declare_blockers`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — Casting pipeline. `cast_spell` does NOT fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent. Pushes StackObject at end; `card.colors_spent = list(...last_payment_colors)`. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` exists. `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets`. Cost reduction via `get_cost_reduction` clamps to generic only.\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — Class hierarchy. Creature has base_power/base_toughness/modified_power/modified_toughness/`power`/`toughness` properties/plus_one_counters/`_base_plus_one_counters`. `_reset_characteristics` resets card_types/keywords (Creature also P/T, counters, `_cant_attack`/`_cant_block`/`_cant_be_blocked`/`_cant_activate`, protections=[]). Land: `can_cast()->False`, `get_mana_abilities()->[]`. Planeswalker: `get_loyalty_abilities()->[]`, `loyalty`/`starting_loyalty`. Dataclasses: Mode, ActivatedAbility(cost,effect,desc), LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost,effect,desc), ManaAbility(cost,mana_produced,desc), ContinuousEffect.\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — All events defined including SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell,player,card,controller), AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature,attacker), EndStepTriggeredEvent(player) — these THREE are never fired. MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination,controller,owner,prevented; `.card` property) + subtypes CreatureDies/PermanentDestroyed/Sacrifice (each with `.card`).\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py` — Helpers: deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice, exile, draw_card (tracks cards_drawn_this_turn, fires DrawsCard), discard, create_token (fires ETB then registers triggers), add_counter (supports \"+1/+1\",\"-1/-1\",\"loyalty\",generic), remove_counter, tap, untap.\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — run_turn dispatches step handlers. UPKEEP fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()`. END step (Step.END) has NO handler. `_NO_PRIORITY_STEPS` = {(BEGINNING,UNTAP),(ENDING,CLEANUP)}. `_do_untap_step` unconditionally untaps + sets land_plays_remaining=1.\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — `declare_attackers_step` taps attackers (unless VIGILANCE), sets is_attacking; does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent. `_can_block` enforces flying/reach.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` — `advance_phase` pops `extra_turns` FIFO else `_normal_next_index`. `_TURN_SEQUENCE` includes (ENDING, Step.END) then (ENDING, Step.CLEANUP).\n   - `/workspace/engine/stack.py` — StackObject(source,controller,targets,on_resolve,is_mana_ability). `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` shallow-copies source for spell copies (casualty). priority_loop.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_205/card_impl.py` — Converge: `self.colors_spent: int = 0`; on_resolve uses `count = self.colors_spent` for token count. (NOTE divergence: engine sets colors_spent to a LIST; this card treats it as int — tests set it directly.)\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_153/card_impl.py` — Counterspell pattern: `_get_chosen_target(card, game)` reads `chosen_targets[0]` else `_resolve_target`; `_counter_spell(game, stack_obj)` removes from `game.stack._items`, removes card from controller STACK zone, adds to owner graveyard. `can_cast` checks stack; `get_targets` returns TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK).\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_44/card_impl.py` — Planeswalker (Kaito): `register_triggers` registers TriggerRegistration watching DealsDamageTriggeredEvent and SpellCastTriggeredEvent (emblem). `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns `[LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost=+1, effect=_plus1, description=...), ...]`. Effects read `pw._resolve_target`. Confirms SpellCastTriggeredEvent firing is expected by reference cards.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_157/card_impl.py` — Surveil 2 inline pattern (copy this): `top_cards = cards[-min(2,len): ]`; `for card in reversed(top_cards): if controller.choose_yes_no(...): library.remove(card); controller.zones[Zone.GRAVEYARD].add(card)`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/spg_82/card_impl.py` — Extra turn: find controller's index, `game.extra_turns.append(player_index)`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/stubs/sos_stubs.py` — Auto-generated stubs (8820 lines, in `cards/stubs/` — NOT the files I edit). Confirms base classes/constructor signatures and that stubs set `self.colors = ['W']` list attribute.\n   - `/workspace/engine_tests/test_casting.py` — Read fully. CRITICAL assertions my engine changes must not break: `test_cast_creature_full_lifecycle` requires `len(game.stack.objects()) == 1` after cast (safe since no SpellCast trigger registered there); `test_on_cast_called_before_push_to_stack`; `test_cast_with_targets_passes_to_stack_object` (`game.stack.peek().targets`).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `python` not found → use `python3` (Python 3.11.2) or `/usr/local/bin/pytest`. No other errors; all actions were reads/greps.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed baseline `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` = **1145 passed, 24 warnings**. Must keep this green.\n   - Confirmed SpellCastTriggeredEvent / AttacksTriggeredEvent / EndStepTriggeredEvent are never fired — must wire them up (SpellCast after StackObject push in cast_spell/cast_spell_free; Attacks in declare_attackers_step; End-step optional). Verified test_casting.py won't break because those tests register no matching triggers.\n   - No existing coin-flip or skip-turn infra; will need to add for Ral's −7. Extra turns model = `game.extra_turns.append(index)`. Surveil = inline `choose_yes_no` loop (fdn_157 pattern). Converge uses `self.colors_spent` (fdn_205 treats as int).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (System reminders re-establishing context: run_manifest.json card_filter [1,4,13,57,97,120,201,226,245,257] benchmark_set \"sos\"; prompt.md; PROJECT_MAP.md; test_utils.md.) The core task from prompt.md (verbatim constraints): \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. **Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.**\"\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (after ToolSearch loaded TaskCreate/TaskUpdate