{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (Strixhaven/MTG set) card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`, filling in the `pass`-stub `card_impl.py` for each. The class names are predetermined and MUST remain in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. Verbatim task from prompt.md: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n\n   Cards (name / type / cost / P-T / oracle):\n   - **SOS 1 — TheDawningArchaic** (Creature {10} 7/7 Avatar LEGENDARY, Reach): costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard; Reach; when it attacks, you may cast target instant/sorcery from graveyard free; if that spell would go to graveyard, exile instead.\n   - **SOS 4 — TogetherAsOne** (Sorcery {6}, Converge): Target player draws X, deals X damage to any target, you gain X life; X = colors of mana spent.\n   - **SOS 13 — EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares** (Creature {1}{W}{W} 3/3 Cat Cleric, NOT legendary per stub): ETB target player creates 1/1 W/B flying Inkling token; then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, becomes prepared; while prepared may cast copy of Swords to Plowshares ({W}: exile target creature, its controller gains life = its power), doing so unprepares it.\n   - **SOS 57 — ManaSculpt** (Instant {1}{U}{U}): Counter target spell; if you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\n   - **SOS 97 — RalZarekGuestLecturer** (Planeswalker {1}{B}{B} Ral LEGENDARY, loyalty 3): +1 Surveil 2; −1 any number of target players each discard; −2 return target creature card MV≤3 from your graveyard to battlefield; −7 flip five coins, target opponent skips next X turns (X=heads).\n   - **SOS 120 — ImprovisationCapstone** (Sorcery {5}{R}{R} Lesson, Paradigm): exile from top of library until total MV≥4; may cast any number of them free; Paradigm.\n   - **SOS 201 — LoreholdTheHistorian** (Creature {3}{R}{W} 5/5 Elder Dragon LEGENDARY, Flying+Haste): instants/sorceries in hand have miracle {2}; at each opponent's upkeep, may discard then draw.\n   - **SOS 226 — SilverquillTheDisputant** (Creature {2}{W}{B} 4/4 Elder Dragon LEGENDARY, Flying+Vigilance): each instant/sorcery you cast has casualty 1.\n   - **SOS 245 — WitherbloomTheBalancer** (Creature {6}{B}{G} 5/5 Elder Dragon LEGENDARY, Deathtouch+Flying): affinity for creatures (self); flying, deathtouch; your instants/sorceries have affinity for creatures.\n   - **SOS 257 — GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex** (Land, empty cost): {T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: add one mana of any color (spend only on instant/sorcery). {5}: if not a creature, becomes 2/4 Wizard creature with \"whenever you cast an instant/sorcery, this gets +1/+0 EOT\"; still a land.\n\n   Also: write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (≤30 tests each) and run full suite. Engine modifications must be additive-only (may add methods/classes/files and modify existing function bodies; MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine items). Treat `engine_tests/` and existing FDN `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` as read-only.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pure-Python (stdlib only) MTG rules engine; bare package imports from workspace root.\n   - CardImpl hooks: can_cast(game), cost_reduction(game)->int (generic-only, clamped≥0), NEW static_cost_reduction(game, spell, controller)->int, on_cast(game), on_resolve(game) (targets via self.chosen_targets), get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement], register_triggers(game), register_replacement_effects(game), get_activated_abilities()->list[ActivatedAbility], get_modes(). Planeswalker: get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]. Land: get_mana_abilities()->list[ManaAbility], can_cast()->False.\n   - Triggers: TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition(game,event)->bool, effect, source, controller). fire_event matches isinstance (subclass-aware), pushes StackObject(source, controller, on_resolve=effect) in APNAP order. NEW: fire_event now wraps effects accepting 2 positional params to pass the event.\n   - Replacement effects: ONLY consulted in move_to_zone when leaving battlefield AND replacement_event supplied. Stack→graveyard (spell resolution) does NOT consult them.\n   - Continuous effects: EffectManager.add(ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)); Layer enum (COPY=1..POWER_TOUGHNESS=7); SubLayer (MODIFY_PT=\"7c\" etc.); DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0, DURATION_PERMANENT=-1; apply_all resets battlefield via _reset_characteristics then reapplies.\n   - Mana: ManaPool.last_payment_colors (distinct Colors, sorted, colorless excluded). cast_spell sets card.colors_spent=list(last_payment_colors). ManaCost.cmc treats X as 0. ManaPool.total() sums pool.\n   - cast_spell (timing+mana), cast_spell_free (no timing/mana, from any zone, finds card in any player's from_zone).\n   - StackObject(source, controller, targets, on_resolve, is_mana_ability). copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets) shallow-copies source, binds on_resolve to copied_card.on_resolve (no zone movement). Stack is LIFO.\n   - game.extra_turns (FIFO seat indices); NEW game.skip_turns dict.\n   - DeterministicPlayer pops scripted answers via _pop(); methods choose_target/choose/choose_yes_no/assign_damage_order/choose_card all pop; remaining_choices property. test_utils.cast_spell scripts targets reversed via player._script.appendleft(target).\n   - Loyalty activation: abilities.py activate_ability → _activate_loyalty_ability (sorcery-speed, once-per-turn via module _loyalty_activated_this_turn, pays loyalty, pushes StackObject(on_resolve=ability.effect)). FDN loyalty effects read targets via getattr(pw,'_resolve_target',None).\n   - move_to_zone fires EntersBattlefield BEFORE register_triggers, so a card's OWN ETB trigger won't self-fire — established pattern: put own-ETB logic in on_resolve (runs in _resolve_spell while card still in STACK zone).\n   - Two ability representations: card.py ActivatedAbility/LoyaltyAbility/ManaAbility dataclasses (cost, effect, description) vs abilities.py ActivatedAbilityInstance/LoyaltyAbilityInstance. activate_ability takes the Instance variants. (Still need to confirm the converter/test pattern — last grep was investigating this.)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — EDITED. In get_cost_reduction, after computing `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)` and restoring controller, added:\n     ```python\n     for player in game.players:\n         for perm in player.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD].get_all():\n             if perm is card:\n                 continue\n             hook = getattr(perm, \"static_cost_reduction\", None)\n             if hook is None:\n                 continue\n             raw += hook(game, card, controller)\n     generic = card.mana_cost.generic if card.mana_cost else 0\n     return max(0, min(raw, generic))\n     ```\n     In cast_spell after payment:\n     ```python\n     pool_total_before = player.mana_pool.total()\n     player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)\n     card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)\n     card.mana_spent = pool_total_before - player.mana_pool.total()\n     ```\n     After `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` (cast_spell):\n     ```python\n     from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n     game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))\n     ```\n     In cast_spell_free: added `card.mana_spent = 0` before on_cast, and the same SpellCastTriggeredEvent fire after push.\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — EDITED. Added to CardImpl after cost_reduction:\n     ```python\n     def static_cost_reduction(self, game: GameState, spell: \"CardImpl\", controller: Player) -> int:\n         return 0\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — EDITED. In declare_attackers_step, collect declared attackers into `declared` list, then after the loop:\n     ```python\n     if declared:\n         from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\n         for attacker in declared:\n             game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/triggers.py` — EDITED. Added `import inspect` and helper `_effect_accepts_event(effect)` (returns True if effect has VAR_POSITIONAL or ≥2 positional params). In fire_event's push loop:\n     ```python\n     effect = trigger.effect\n     if _effect_accepts_event(effect):\n         def _on_resolve(g: GameState, _effect=effect, _event=event) -> None:\n             _effect(g, _event)\n         resolve_cb = _on_resolve\n     else:\n         resolve_cb = effect\n     stack_obj = StackObject(source=trigger.source, controller=trigger.controller, on_resolve=resolve_cb)\n     game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — EDITED. Added after EndStepTriggeredEvent:\n     ```pyt