{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (Strixhaven) MTG card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`, filling in the `pass`-stub `card_impl.py` for each. Verbatim task from prompt.md: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   Also required: write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (≤30 tests each) and run the full suite. Engine modifications must be additive-only (may add methods/classes/files and modify existing function bodies; MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine items). The card class names are predetermined and MUST remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`.\n\n   Cards (name / type / cost / P-T / oracle):\n   - **SOS 1 — TheDawningArchaic** (Creature {10} 7/7 Avatar LEGENDARY): costs {1} less per instant/sorcery card in your graveyard; Reach; \"Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n   - **SOS 4 — TogetherAsOne** (Sorcery {6}, Converge): Target player draws X, deals X damage to any target, you gain X life; X = number of colors of mana spent to cast it.\n   - **SOS 13 — EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares** (Creature {1}{W}{W} 3/3 Cat Cleric, NOT legendary): ETB target player creates a 1/1 white-and-black Inkling token with flying; then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this becomes prepared; prepare spell = Swords to Plowshares ({W} instant: exile target creature, its controller gains life equal to its power); casting it unprepares this.\n   - **SOS 57 — ManaSculpt** (Instant {1}{U}{U}): Counter target spell; if you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to the mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\n   - **SOS 97 — RalZarekGuestLecturer** (Planeswalker {1}{B}{B} Ral LEGENDARY, loyalty 3): +1 Surveil 2; −1 any number of target players each discard a card; −2 return target creature card MV≤3 from your graveyard to the battlefield; −7 flip five coins, target opponent skips next X turns (X = heads).\n   - **SOS 120 — ImprovisationCapstone** (Sorcery {5}{R}{R} Lesson, Paradigm): exile from top of library until total MV≥4; may cast any number of them free; Paradigm.\n   - **SOS 201 — LoreholdTheHistorian** (Creature {3}{R}{W} 5/5 Elder Dragon LEGENDARY): Flying, haste; instants/sorceries in your hand have miracle {2}; at the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\n   - **SOS 226 — SilverquillTheDisputant** (Creature {2}{W}{B} 4/4 Elder Dragon LEGENDARY): Flying, vigilance; each instant/sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1.\n   - **SOS 245 — WitherbloomTheBalancer** (Creature {6}{B}{G} 5/5 Elder Dragon LEGENDARY): Affinity for creatures (self, {1} less per creature you control); Flying, deathtouch; instants/sorceries you cast have affinity for creatures.\n   - **SOS 257 — GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex** (Land, no cost): {T}: Add {C}. {T},Pay 1 life: add one mana of any color (spend only on instant/sorcery). {5}: if not a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn\"; still a land.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pure-Python (stdlib only) MTG rules engine; flat imports from workspace root (conftest.py puts workspace on sys.path).\n   - CardImpl hooks: can_cast, cost_reduction(game)->int (generic-only, clamped≥0), static_cost_reduction(game, spell, controller)->int (NEW, summed across battlefield permanents in get_cost_reduction), on_cast, on_resolve (targets via self.chosen_targets), get_targets->list[TargetRequirement], register_triggers, register_replacement_effects, get_activated_abilities->list[ActivatedAbility], get_modes. Planeswalker: get_loyalty_abilities->list[LoyaltyAbility]. Land: get_mana_abilities->list[ManaAbility], can_cast->False.\n   - TWO ability representations: card.py dataclasses `ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description)`, `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`, `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` — returned by card hooks. abilities.py runtime `ActivatedAbilityInstance(source, controller, cost, effect, is_mana_ability=False, description=\"\")` and `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source, controller, loyalty_cost=0, effect, description=\"\")` — passed to `activate_ability(game, player, ability)`. Tests construct the Instance forms manually from the dataclass cost/effect callables.\n   - `activate_ability`: mana abilities (is_mana_ability=True) call effect immediately; regular push StackObject(on_resolve=effect); loyalty requires sorcery speed + once-per-turn (module set `_loyalty_activated_this_turn` keyed by (object_id, turn_number)), pays loyalty (AbilityError if <0), pushes StackObject. `clear_loyalty_tracking()` resets. `tap_cost(game, source)` taps if untapped.\n   - Triggers: TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition(game,event)->bool|None, effect, source, controller). fire_event matches isinstance (subclass-aware), pushes StackObject in APNAP order. NEW: fire_event wraps effects accepting ≥2 positional params (or VAR_POSITIONAL) to pass the event as `effect(game, event)`; 1-arg effects called as `effect(game)`.\n   - Events: SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller); AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker); BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (no fields); EndStepTriggeredEvent(player); MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent(player) (NEW); EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent; DealsDamageTriggeredEvent(source, target, amount, is_combat, combat); etc.\n   - Replacement effects: ONLY consulted in move_to_zone when leaving battlefield AND replacement_event supplied. Stack→graveyard (spell resolution in `_resolve_spell`) does NOT consult them — so Dawning Archaic's \"exile instead\" must use a flag check in `_resolve_spell`.\n   - Continuous effects: `game.effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp=0, duration))`; Layer.TYPE=4, Layer.ABILITY=6, Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS=7; SubLayer.SET_PT=\"7b\", SubLayer.MODIFY_PT=\"7c\"; DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. apply_all resets battlefield via `_reset_characteristics` then reapplies sorted by (layer, sublayer, timestamp). Modify P/T via `obj.modified_power += N`.\n   - Mana: ManaPool.last_payment_colors (distinct Colors, colorless excluded, sorted). cast_spell sets `card.colors_spent = list(last_payment_colors)` and `card.mana_spent = pool_total_before - pool.total()`. ManaCost.cmc treats X as 0. Library top = last element (`library.top(1)` / `cards[-1]`).\n   - cast_spell (timing + mana), cast_spell_free (no timing/mana, from any zone, finds card in any player's from_zone; sets mana_spent=0). Both fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent after push.\n   - StackObject(source, controller, targets, on_resolve, is_mana_ability). copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None) shallow-copies source, binds on_resolve to copied_card.on_resolve (no zone movement). Stack is LIFO.\n   - game.extra_turns (FIFO seat indices), game.skip_turns dict (NEW), `_next_active_player_index` honors skip_turns.\n   - DeterministicPlayer pops scripted answers; test_utils.cast_spell scripts targets via `player._script.appendleft(target)` in reversed order; declare_attackers scripts `active._script.appendleft(attackers_list)`.\n   - No gain_life helper — use `player.life += x`. Counterspell: remove from `game.stack._items`, remove from controller STACK zone, add to owner GRAVEYARD (see fdn_153 `_counter_spell`).\n   - move_to_zone fires EntersBattlefield BEFORE register_triggers, so a card's OWN ETB trigger won't self-fire — put own-ETB logic in on_resolve (runs in _resolve_spell while card still in STACK zone). create_token follows same ordering.\n   - FDN/SOS card_impl.py subclass the proper base type (Creature/Instant/Sorcery/Planeswalker/Land), NOT CardImpl, and have NO registration function. SOS stubs currently subclass CardImpl and must be changed to the proper base.\n   - Mechanics rules confirmed from RULEBOOK.txt: Paradigm (702.192) = first resolution of a same-named spell creates a copy in exile at the beginning of each of your precombat main phases for the rest of the game, castable free; \"Exile this spell.\" Prepared (722.3a-c): permanent with a prepare spell becomes prepared; a copy of the prepare spell is created in exile; controller may cast it; casting loses the prepared designation; unprepared removes designation.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — EDITED (prior session, confirmed intact). get_cost_reduction sums `static_cost_reduction` across battlefield permanents (skipping the card itself), clamps to generic. cast_spell sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` and `card.mana_spent = pool_total_before - player.mana_pool.total()`, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent after push. cast_spell_free sets `card.mana_spent = 0`, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent. STILL NEEDS edit: in `_resolve_spell`, non-permanent branch should be `dest = Zone.EXILE if getattr(card, \"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\", False) else Zone.GRAVEYARD; move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, dest)`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — EDITED (confirmed). Added `static_cost_reduction(self, game, spell, controller) -> int` returning 0.\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — EDITED (prior). declare_attackers_step collects `declared` and fires AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker) for each.\n   - `/workspace/engine/triggers.py` — EDITED (confirmed). Added `import inspect`, helper `_effect_accepts_event(effect)`, and wraps 2-param effects in fire_event push loop.\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — EDITED (confirmed). Added `MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent(player)`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — EDITED (confirmed). Fires MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent on main phases and EndStepTriggeredEvent on END step.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` — EDITED (confirmed). Added `self.skip_turns: dict[int,int] = {}`; `_next_active_player_index` honors skip_turns.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_95/card_impl.py` — activated ability pattern (`get_activated_abilities` returns `[ActivatedAbility(cost=_cost, effect=_effect, description=...)]`, `_cost(game, src)` pays mana via `controller.mana_pool.pay(ManaCost.parse(...))`, effect reads `source._current_target`).\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_44/card_impl.py` — planeswalker pattern (register_triggers + get_loyalty_abilities returning `LoyaltyAbility` list; effects read `getattr(pw, '_resolve_target', None)`; emblem via `type('Emblem', (), {'name':...})()`).\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_153/card_impl.py` — counterspell pattern (`_get_chosen_target`, `_counter_spell`, can_cast checks stack, get_targets TargetRequirement zone=Zone.STACK).\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_205/card_impl.py` + `tests.py` — Converge pattern: `self.colors_spent: int = 0`; on_resolve uses `count = self.colors_spent`. Test sets `card.colors_spent = N` (int) directly and calls on_resolve, imports `from cards.fdn.fdn_205.card_impl import WardensOfTheCycle`, uses `from test_utils import create_game`. MY Converge card must handle colors_spent being int OR list: `cs = getattr(self,'colors_spent',0); x = cs if isinstance(cs,int) else len(cs)`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_157/card_impl.py` — Surveil 2 inline (`top_cards = cards[-min(2,len(cards)):]`, reversed, choose_yes_no → library.remove + graveyard.add).\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_6/card_impl.py` — Affinity via cost_reduction counting subtypes; until-EOT buff via ContinuousEffect(Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, DURATION_END_OF_TURN).\n   - `/workspace/engine_tests/test_abilities.py` — authoritative invocation patterns for ActivatedAbilityInstance / LoyaltyAbilityInstance + activate_ability (READ ONLY — do not modify).\n   - All 10 `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` — still `class X(CardImpl): pass`. Class names confirmed: TheDawningArchaic, TogetherAsOne, EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares, ManaSculpt, RalZarekGuestLecturer, ImprovisationCapstone, LoreholdTheHistorian, SilverquillTheDisputant, WitherbloomTheBalancer, GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex.\n   - All 10 `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_spec.json` — READ (oracle text/types/costs confirmed above).\n   - `/workspace/cards/stubs/sos_stubs.py` (partial) — reference constructors confirmed for cards 1/4/13/57/97; Emeritus stub does NOT set LEGENDARY (correct) and sets `self.colors = ['W']`; Ral stub sets subtypes {'Ral'}, LEGENDARY, starting_loyalty=3, colors=['B'].\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors this session (pure investigation). Note from prior session: `python` is not available in this env — must use `python3` or `/usr/local/bin/pytest`. Baseline `pytest engine_tests/ -q` → 1145 passed.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed the ActivatedAbility/LoyaltyAbility/ManaAbility dataclass (card hooks) vs ActivatedAbilityInstance/LoyaltyAbilityInstance (activate_ability) split; tests must construct the Instance variants.\n   - Confirmed colors_spent dual-form (int via test backdoor, list via real cast) — Converge card must handle both.\n   - Confirmed library \"top\" = last list element (relevant for Dawning Archaic / Improvisation Capstone / Surveil).\n   - Confirmed no gain_life helper (use `player.life += x`).\n   - Confirmed replacement effects don't fire on stack→graveyard, requiring the `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` flag in `_resolve_spell` (still pending).\n   - Confirmed RULEBOOK definitions for Paradigm and Prepared.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - System reminders re-establishing the Read tool results for engine files (game_state.py, turn.py, events.py, triggers.py) and the deferred-tools/ToolSearch note (the resumption context).\n   - Continuation instruction: \"Continue the conversation from where it left off... Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\"\n   - Final CRITICAL instruction: \"Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n   - Preserved constraints (verbatim, still in effect): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\" Additive-only engine rule: \"You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions... You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/`.\" Max 30 tests per card. Card class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Task #1 (in_progress, nearly done): add `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` flag handling to `_resolve_spell` in casting.py.\n   - Tasks #2–#11: Implement each of the 10 SOS cards (all still `pass` stubs) — change base class from CardImpl to the proper type and fill in mechanics.\n   - Task #12: Write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (≤30 each) and run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ cards/ -q` (or `/usr/local/bin/pytest`).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I was completing the engine-API discovery phase needed before writing card code. I had just read all ability/mana/loyalty invocation patterns (basic_lands.py, abilities.py, card.py, test_abilities.py, fdn_95, fdn_44, fdn_153, fdn_205+tests, fdn_157, fdn_6), all engine support modules (continuous_effects.py, types.py, mana.py, stack.py, player.py, game.py, casting.py, test_utils.py, conftest.py), all 10 SOS card_spec.json files, confirmed all 10 SOS class names via grep, read the SOS stubs reference constructors (partial), and finally ran a Bash grep of RULEBOOK.txt for \"prepared|paradigm|swords to plowshares\" which returned rule 702.192 (Paradigm) and rules 722.3a-c (Prepared/unprepared). No SOS card_impl.py has been written or edited yet in this session; all engine edits from the prior session are confirmed intact and 1145 engine tests pass.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Add the `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` flag to `_resolve_spell` in `/workspace/engine/casting.py` (change the non-permanent branch to: `dest = Zone.EXILE if getattr(card, \"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\", False) else Zone.GRAVEYARD; move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, dest)`), then begin writing the SOS card implementations starting with the simplest (SOS 245 Witherbloom: keywords FLYING|DEATHTOUCH, cost_reduction = creatures you control, static_cost_reduction granting affinity-for-creatures to your instants/sorceries; SOS 226 Silverquill: FLYING|VIGILANCE + casualty-1 trigger via copy_spell; SOS 4 Together as One: Converge X = colors spent; SOS 57 Mana Sculpt: counterspell + Wizard-conditioned delayed mana), changing each base class from CardImpl to the proper type. This is directly in line with the explicit task \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`\" and the just-completed investigation into activated/mana/loyalty ability invocation (for SOS 257, SOS 13, SOS 97) and Paradigm/Prepared rules. After implementations, write per-card tests (≤30 each) and run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ cards/ -q`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/f8a3aed6-12f8-4341-9631-2336f98abe5d.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8a3aed6-12f8-4341-9631-2336f98abe5d","uuid":"a61ef7a6-2d42-4a74-bfce-6b83fb7d880c","timestamp":"2026-06-04T06:14:39.137Z","isSynthetic":true}
