{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Verbatim task (from prompt.md, established in prior session and still in effect): \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   Also required: write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (≤30 tests each) and run the full suite (`python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ cards/ -q` or `/usr/local/bin/pytest`; note `python` is NOT available, use `python3`).\n   Engine modifications MUST be additive-only: \"You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions... You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/`.\" Card class names are predetermined and MUST remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. Baseline: `pytest engine_tests/ -q` → 1145 passed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pure-Python (stdlib only) MTG rules engine; flat imports from workspace root (conftest.py adds /workspace to sys.path).\n   - CardImpl hooks: can_cast(game)->bool, cost_reduction(game)->int (generic-only, clamped≥0), static_cost_reduction(game, spell, controller)->int (summed across ALL battlefield permanents in get_cost_reduction, skipping the spell itself), on_cast(game), on_resolve(game) (targets via self.chosen_targets), get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement], register_triggers(game), register_replacement_effects(game), get_activated_abilities()->list[ActivatedAbility], get_modes(). Planeswalker.get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]. Land.get_mana_abilities()->list[ManaAbility], Land.can_cast()->False.\n   - TWO ability representations: card.py dataclasses `ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description)`, `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`, `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` returned by card hooks; abilities.py runtime `ActivatedAbilityInstance(source, controller, cost, effect, is_mana_ability=False, description=\"\")` and `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source, controller, loyalty_cost=0, effect, description=\"\")` passed to `activate_ability(game, player, ability)`. Tests construct the Instance forms from the dataclass cost/effect callables.\n   - activate_ability: mana abilities (is_mana_ability=True) call effect(game) immediately (bypass timing); regular push StackObject(on_resolve=effect); loyalty requires sorcery speed + once-per-turn (module set `_loyalty_activated_this_turn` keyed by (object_id, turn_number)), pays loyalty (AbilityError if new_loyalty<0), pushes StackObject. `clear_loyalty_tracking()` resets. `tap_cost(game, source)` taps if untapped, returns bool.\n   - Targeting conventions: spells read `self.chosen_targets` (set by _resolve_spell from StackObject.targets) — helper `_get_chosen_target(card, game)` falls back to `getattr(card, \"_resolve_target\", None)`. Activated abilities read `source._current_target` (fdn_95). Loyalty abilities read `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_target\", None)` (fdn_44). I will define `pw._resolve_targets` (list) for multi-target Ral −1.\n   - Triggers: TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition(game,event)->bool|None, effect, source, controller). fire_event matches isinstance (subclass-aware), pushes StackObject in APNAP order. fire_event wraps effects accepting ≥2 positional params (or VAR_POSITIONAL) to pass the event as `effect(game, event)`; 1-arg effects called as `effect(game)`. unregister(source) is identity-based.\n   - Events: SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=StackObject, player, card, controller); AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker); BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (NO fields — fired during active player's upkeep, so determine whose upkeep via game.active_player); EndStepTriggeredEvent(player); MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent(player) (fired for BOTH precombat and postcombat main; distinguish via game.phase==Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN); DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card); EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent; CreatureDiesTriggeredEvent; DealsDamageTriggeredEvent(source, target, amount, is_combat, combat).\n   - move_to_zone fires EntersBattlefield BEFORE register_triggers, so a card's OWN ETB trigger won't self-fire — put own-ETB logic in on_resolve (runs in _resolve_spell while card still in STACK zone). create_token follows the same ordering. When on_resolve runs the card is on the STACK, not battlefield (matters for \"creatures you control\" counts — e.g. Emeritus must count itself with +1).\n   - Replacement effects ONLY consulted in move_to_zone when leaving battlefield AND replacement_event supplied. Stack→graveyard (spell resolution) does NOT consult them — hence the `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` flag added to `_resolve_spell` (now done).\n   - Continuous effects: `game.effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp=0, duration))`; Layer.TYPE=4, Layer.ABILITY=6, Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS=7; SubLayer.SET_PT=\"7b\", SubLayer.MODIFY_PT=\"7c\"; DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. apply_all resets battlefield via `_reset_characteristics` (CardImpl resets card_types→_original_card_types and keywords→_original_keywords; Creature also resets modified_power/toughness/counters) then reapplies sorted by (layer, sublayer-order, timestamp). Modify P/T via `obj.modified_power += N`. CRITICAL for Land animation: card_types are reset to {LAND} each apply_all, so animation must be a permanent TYPE-layer ContinuousEffect that re-adds CREATURE/Wizard each cycle; Land has no power/toughness/_reset of P/T by default.\n   - Mana: ManaPool.last_payment_colors (distinct Colors, colorless excluded, sorted by Color.value). cast_spell sets `card.colors_spent = list(last_payment_colors)` and `card.mana_spent = pool_total_before - pool.total()`. ManaCost.cmc treats X as 0; hybrid contributes 1 each. ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{U}{U}\"). Library top = last element (`library.top(1)` returns last n; `_objects[-1]` is top). move_zone deletes stale colors_spent on any zone change. cast_spell deletes colors_spent before payment.\n   - cast_spell (timing + mana, from hand), cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone) (no timing/mana, finds card in any player's from_zone; sets mana_spent=0). Both fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent AFTER pushing StackObject (so casualty/cast triggers go ON TOP of the spell).\n   - copy_spell(game, original_stackobj, controller, new_targets=None) shallow-copies source, binds on_resolve to copied_card.on_resolve (no zone movement). Stack is LIFO. game.stack._items is the underlying list (used by _counter_spell to remove from middle).\n   - game.extra_turns (FIFO seat indices), game.skip_turns dict[int,int] keyed by seat index (honored in _next_active_player_index — decrements and skips).\n   - No gain_life helper — use `player.life += x`. Counterspell pattern (fdn_153 _counter_spell): remove StackObject from game.stack._items, remove card from controller STACK zone, add to owner GRAVEYARD.\n   - DeterministicPlayer pops scripted answers (deque, popleft); ScriptExhaustedError when empty. test_utils.cast_spell scripts targets via `player._script.appendleft(target)` in reversed order; declare_attackers scripts `active._script.appendleft(attackers_list)`; declare_blockers scripts `defending._script.appendleft(block_map)`. GUARD all player choices in card code with try/except (ScriptExhaustedError, NotImplementedError) to avoid breaking full games.\n   - FDN/SOS card_impl.py subclass the proper base type (Creature/Instant/Sorcery/Planeswalker/Land), NOT CardImpl; NO registration function. SOS stubs currently `class X(CardImpl): pass` and must be changed to the proper base.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — EDITED this session (Task #13 complete). The non-permanent resolution branch in `_resolve_spell` now reads:\n     ```python\n     else:\n         dest = (\n             Zone.EXILE\n             if getattr(card, \"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\", False)\n             else Zone.GRAVEYARD\n         )\n         move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, dest)\n     ```\n     Also confirmed: get_cost_reduction sums `hook(game, card, controller)` for `static_cost_reduction` across all battlefield permanents (skipping `perm is card`), then `return max(0, min(raw, generic))`. cast_spell sets colors_spent (list) and mana_spent, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent. cast_spell_free sets `card.mana_spent = 0`, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent.\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — confirmed intact: `static_cost_reduction(self, game, spell, controller) -> int` returns 0 by default; Creature has base_power/base_toughness/modified_power/modified_toughness, power/toughness properties (modified ± counters), summoning_sick default True; Land.can_cast→False, get_mana_abilities→[]; Planeswalker.starting_loyalty/loyalty, get_loyalty_abilities→[].\n   - `/workspace/engine/triggers.py`, `events.py`, `turn.py`, `game_state.py`, `combat.py` — confirmed prior edits intact (event wrapping helper, MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent, EndStep/MainPhase firing, skip_turns, AttacksTriggeredEvent firing).\n   - `/workspace/cards/stubs/sos_stubs.py` — reference constructors (use these exact name/cost/types in card_impl __init__ setdefaults):\n     - TheDawningArchaic(Creature): name 'The Dawning Archaic', {10}, subtypes {'Avatar'}, LEGENDARY, 7/7.\n     - TogetherAsOne(Sorcery): {6}, no subtypes/colors set.\n     - EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature): {1}{W}{W}, subtypes {'Cat','Cleric'}, 3/3, NOT legendary, self.colors=['W'].\n     - ManaSculpt(Instant): {1}{U}{U}, self.colors=['U'].\n     - RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker): {1}{B}{B}, subtypes {'Ral'}, LEGENDARY, starting_loyalty=3, self.colors=['B'].\n     - ImprovisationCapstone(Sorcery): {5}{R}{R}, subtypes {'Lesson'}, self.colors=['R'].\n     - LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature): {3}{R}{W}, subtypes {'Elder','Dragon'}, LEGENDARY, 5/5, self.colors=['R','W'].\n     - SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature): {2}{W}{B}, subtypes {'Elder','Dragon'}, LEGENDARY, 4/4, self.colors=['B','W'].\n     - WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature): {6}{B}{G}, subtypes {'Elder','Dragon'}, LEGENDARY, 5/5, self.colors=['B','G'].\n     - GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land): name 'Great Hall of the Biblioplex', mana_cost ManaCost(), card_types {LAND}, no colors.\n   - All 10 `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_spec.json` — read; oracle text confirmed (see Primary Request mappings in prior summary; key details: SOS 1 Reach + attack-cast-from-gy-exile-instead; SOS 4 Converge X=colors; SOS 13 Inkling token + prepared/Swords to Plowshares; SOS 57 counter + Wizard-conditioned delayed {C}; SOS 97 four loyalty abilities; SOS 120 exile-until-MV4 + Paradigm; SOS 201 flying/haste + miracle{2} + opponent-upkeep loot; SOS 226 flying/vigilance + casualty 1; SOS 245 affinity-for-creatures self + grant to instants/sorceries + flying/deathtouch; SOS 257 mana abilities + {5} animate to 2/4 Wizard).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` — read; still `class TheDawningArchaic(CardImpl): pass` (representative of all 10 stubs which all still need implementing).\n   - FDN reference cards (patterns to copy): fdn_6 (cost_reduction affinity + ContinuousEffect EOT pump), fdn_44 (Planeswalker register_triggers + get_loyalty_abilities, _resolve_target, emblem via `type('Emblem', (), {'name':...})()`), fdn_95 (get_activated_abilities returning ActivatedAbility, `_cost(game, src)` pays mana, effect reads `source._current_target`), fdn_153 (counterspell can_cast/get_targets/_counter_spell/_get_chosen_target), fdn_205 + tests.py (Converge: `self.colors_spent: int = 0`, on_resolve `count = self.colors_spent`; test sets `card.colors_spent = N` and calls on_resolve directly, imports `from cards.fdn.fdn_205.card_impl import WardensOfTheCycle`, `from test_utils import create_game`).\n   - `/workspace/test_utils.py` and `/workspace/conftest.py` — test harness; create_game(deck1, deck2, scripts=(s1,s2)), set_board_state(game, idx, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana={ManaType:n}), cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=), declare_attackers(game, [names]), declare_blockers(game, {atk:[blk]}).\n   - `/workspace/engine_tests/test_abilities.py` — authoritative ActivatedAbilityInstance/LoyaltyAbilityInstance + activate_ability test patterns (DO NOT MODIFY).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors this session (verification + one successful Edit). Prior-session note still applies: `python` binary unavailable — use `python3` or `/usr/local/bin/pytest`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Completed the `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` flag in `_resolve_spell` (needed for SOS 1 Dawning Archaic and SOS 120 Paradigm self-exile).\n   - Confirmed BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent has NO player field → Lorehold's \"each opponent's upkeep\" must check game.active_player is not controller.\n   - Confirmed MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent fires for both main phases → SOS 57 delayed {C} and SOS 120 Paradigm must filter by player and (for Paradigm) game.phase==PRECOMBAT_MAIN.\n   - Identified Land-animation challenge (SOS 257): apply_all resets card_types to {LAND}; animation must be a permanent TYPE-layer ContinuousEffect re-adding CREATURE/Wizard each cycle; Land lacks creature P/T attributes so they must be initialized/managed (plan: add creature attrs in __init__ and/or via continuous effect, override _reset_characteristics on the card subclass).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - System reminders re-establishing Read results for game_state.py, turn.py, events.py, triggers.py, and the deferred-tools/ToolSearch note (resumption context).\n   - \"Continue the conversation from where it left off... Pick up the last task as if the break never happened. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary...\"\n   - Recurring system task-reminders listing tasks #1–#13.\n   - Final CRITICAL instruction: \"Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n   - Preserved constraints (verbatim, still in effect): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\" Additive-only: \"You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions... You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/`.\" Max 30 tests per card. Card class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Task #1 (in_progress): broader engine wiring (mostly complete — events, triggers, skip_turns, static_cost_reduction, MainPhaseBegan all done; may mark complete).\n   - Tasks #2–#11: Implement each of the 10 SOS cards (all still `class X(CardImpl): pass` — change base class to proper type, fill mechanics).\n   - Task #12: Write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (≤30 each) and run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ cards/ -q`.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary I was in the final design-analysis phase, having just grepped combat.py (confirmed `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker)` at line 270, summoning_sick/HASTE check, is_attacking flags). No SOS card_impl.py has been written this session. I had finalized concrete per-card implementation plans:\n   - **SOS 245 Witherbloom** (simplest): subclass Creature, keywords FLYING|DEATHTOUCH; `cost_reduction(game)` = count creatures controller controls; `static_cost_reduction(game, spell, controller)`: if self.controller is controller and spell is INSTANT/SORCERY, return creatures-controlled count.\n   - **SOS 226 Silverquill**: Creature, FLYING|VIGILANCE; register_triggers on SpellCastTriggeredEvent (condition event.controller is self.controller and event.card is instant/sorcery); effect (game, event) offers casualty 1: guarded choose_yes_no, choose creature power≥1, sacrifice(game, controller, creature), then copy_spell(game, event.spell, controller) and game.stack.push(copy).\n   - **SOS 4 Together as One**: Sorcery, `self.colors_spent=0` init; get_targets returns [target player, any target]; on_resolve x = colors_spent (int or len(list)); target_player draws x, deal_damage(self, damage_target, x), controller.life += x.\n   - **SOS 57 Mana Sculpt**: Instant; can_cast requires a spell on stack (not self); get_targets target spell; on_resolve counters via _counter_spell pattern, amount=getattr(countered_card,'mana_spent',0); if controller controls a Wizard, register sentinel-source MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent trigger (condition event.player is controller) that adds {C}×amount then unregisters itself.\n   - **SOS 1 Dawning Archaic**: Creature, REACH; cost_reduction = count instant/sorcery in controller graveyard; register_triggers on AttacksTriggeredEvent (condition event.attacker is self); effect chooses an instant/sorcery in graveyard (guarded), sets chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard=True, cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD).\n   - **SOS 13 Emeritus**: Creature; get_targets target player; on_resolve creates 1/1 W/B flying Inkling token for target player, counts creatures (your count +1 since Emeritus on stack), sets self.is_prepared if opponent has more; nested SwordsToPlowshares(Instant) class exiles chosen_targets[0] and grants its controller life=power; cast_prepared(game, target_creature) pays {W} best-effort, runs StP effect, sets is_prepared=False.\n   - **SOS 97 Ral Zarek**: Planeswalker; get_loyalty_abilities returns 4 LoyaltyAbility: +1 Surveil 2 (top 2 of controller library, guarded choose_yes_no per fdn_157 pattern); −1 read pw._resolve_targets list, each player discards (guarded, default last card); −2 read pw._resolve_target creature card MV≤3 in controller graveyard, move_to_zone to battlefield; −7 flip 5 coins (random; tests seed random), game.skip_turns[opp_seat]+=heads for pw._resolve_target opponent.\n   - **SOS 120 Improvisation Capstone**: Sorcery; on_resolve exiles top of controller library until total MV≥4, then for each may cast_spell_free (guarded); Paradigm: set self._exile_instead_of_graveyard=True + register sentinel MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent trigger (player==controller and PRECOMBAT_MAIN) offering a free copy cast (guarded).\n   - **SOS 201 Lorehold**: Creature, FLYING|HASTE; register_triggers: (a) opponent-upkeep loot on BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (condition active_player is not controller) — guarded discard then draw; (b) miracle on DrawsCardTriggeredEvent (condition event.player is controller, cards_drawn_this_turn==1, card instant/sorcery in hand) — guarded choose_yes_no, pay {2} if can_pay, cast_spell_free.\n   - **SOS 257 Great Hall**: Land; get_mana_abilities: ManaAbility({T}: add C) and ManaAbility({T}+pay 1 life: add any color — restriction is an engine limitation, add mana best-effort); get_activated_abilities: {5} animate via permanent TYPE-layer ContinuousEffect adding CREATURE+Wizard, set 2/4 P/T, register cast-pump trigger (+1/+0 EOT on cast of instant/sorcery you control). Plan to initialize creature attrs on the Land and possibly override _reset_characteristics.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Begin implementing the SOS cards, starting with the simplest (SOS 245 Witherbloom), changing the base class from CardImpl to the proper type and filling in mechanics, then proceeding through SOS 226, 4, 57, 1, 13, 97, 120, 201, 257. This is directly in line with the explicit task: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`.\" After each implementation (or in a batch), write per-card tests (≤30 each) at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`, then run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ cards/ -q` to verify the baseline (1145 engine tests) still passes and the new card tests pass. Mark Task #1 complete (engine wiring done) and update Tasks #2–#12 as progress is made.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/f8a3aed6-12f8-4341-9631-2336f98abe5d.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8a3aed6-12f8-4341-9631-2336f98abe5d","uuid":"896e1d1d-56e9-42f9-a852-c38aac3ac395","timestamp":"2026-06-04T06:23:28.863Z","isSynthetic":true}
