{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Verbatim task (from prompt.md, still in effect): \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   Also required: write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (≤30 tests each) and run the full suite (`python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ cards/ -q` or `/usr/local/bin/pytest`; `python` is NOT available — use `python3`).\n   Engine modifications MUST be additive-only: \"You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions... You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/`.\" Card class names are predetermined and MUST remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. Baseline: `pytest engine_tests/ -q` → 1145 passed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pure-Python (stdlib only) MTG engine; flat imports from /workspace. `python3` only (no `python`).\n   - CardImpl hooks: can_cast(game)->bool (default True); cost_reduction(game)->int (generic-only self-reduction, clamped); static_cost_reduction(game, spell, controller)->int (default 0; summed across ALL battlefield permanents in get_cost_reduction, skipping `perm is card`); on_cast(game); on_resolve(game) (targets via self.chosen_targets, set by _resolve_spell from stack_obj.targets while card is on STACK); get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]; register_triggers(game); register_replacement_effects(game); get_activated_abilities()->list[ActivatedAbility]; get_modes(). Creature adds base_power/base_toughness/modified_power/modified_toughness, power/toughness properties (= modified ± counters), summoning_sick default True, damage_marked, is_attacking/is_blocking, plus_one_counters/minus_one_counters, is_token, dealt_deathtouch_damage. Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=, loyalty); get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]. Land.can_cast→False, get_mana_abilities()->list[ManaAbility] (default []).\n   - card.py dataclasses: ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description); LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description); ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description); Mode(name, description). NOTE: card.py ALSO defines a different ContinuousEffect(apply, remove, description) — DO NOT use it; use engine.continuous_effects.ContinuousEffect.\n   - ManaAbility canonical pattern (basic_lands.py / fdn_267): `cost` is a callable that PAYS the cost and returns bool — either `cost(game)->bool` (Plains form, source captured via closure) or `cost(game, src)->bool` (fdn_267 form); `mana_produced` is a side-effect callable `(game)->None` that adds mana to controller's pool. NOTHING in the engine auto-invokes ManaAbility from get_mana_abilities — tests/cards must call them directly. (fdn_272 Plains uses a `produce(game)->dict` return form but that return is unused; prefer the side-effect form.)\n   - abilities.py: _activate_regular_ability checks `getattr(ability.source,\"_cant_activate\",False)`, calls `cost_paid = ability.cost(game, ability.source)`, then mana abilities call `ability.effect(game)` immediately, regular abilities push StackObject(on_resolve=ability.effect). _activate_loyalty_ability requires is_sorcery_speed + once-per-turn (`_loyalty_activated_this_turn` set keyed by (object_id, turn_number)), pays loyalty (AbilityError if new_loyalty<0), pushes StackObject. clear_loyalty_tracking() clears the set. NOTE: get_activated_abilities/get_loyalty_abilities return the DATACLASSES (ActivatedAbility/LoyaltyAbility), and activation expects ActivatedAbilityInstance/LoyaltyAbilityInstance — for tests, call the dataclass's cost/effect directly: ActivatedAbility cost is `cost(game, src)`, effect is `effect(game)`.\n   - Targeting: cast_spell calls get_targets(game); for each spec, player.choose_target(specs, spec) pops a scripted answer; validates via spec.filter_fn(target) (rollback+CastingError on failure); protection check via has_protection_from; stores chosen list on StackObject.targets. _resolve_spell sets card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets before on_resolve. Per-card helper `_get_chosen_target(card, game)`: returns `chosen_targets[0]` else `getattr(card,\"_resolve_target\",None)`. Activated abilities read `source._current_target` (fdn_95). Loyalty read `getattr(pw,\"_resolve_target\",None)` (fdn_44); plan adds `pw._resolve_targets` (list) for Ral −1. TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone) — zone is NOT used by DeterministicPlayer selection (it just pops scripted answers), so zone can be a placeholder (e.g. Zone.BATTLEFIELD) even for player targets.\n   - Triggers (triggers.py): TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition:(game,event)->bool|None, effect, source, controller). fire_event matches isinstance (subclass-aware), pushes StackObject APNAP-ordered (active player's triggers first/bottom). fire_event WRAPS effects accepting ≥2 positional params (or VAR_POSITIONAL) to call effect(game, event); 1-arg effects called effect(game). unregister(source) identity-based; only auto-called when leaving battlefield in move_to_zone — so a trigger with source = a card in exile/graveyard or a sentinel object PERSISTS.\n   - Events (events.py): SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=StackObject, player, card, controller) fired AFTER pushing the spell's StackObject in BOTH cast_spell and cast_spell_free (copy_spell does NOT fire it). AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker) fired per declared attacker in combat.py:264-271. BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (NO fields — determine whose upkeep via game.active_player). EndStepTriggeredEvent(player). MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent(player) fired for BOTH main phases with player=game.active_player (distinguish via game.phase==Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN). DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card) fired AFTER incrementing player.cards_drawn_this_turn (first card of turn ⇒ cards_drawn_this_turn==1). Also EntersBattlefield, CreatureDies, DealsDamage(source,target,amount,is_combat,combat), LosesLife, GainsLife, CounterAdded.\n   - move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None): fires ETB BEFORE register_triggers (own ETB won't self-fire — put own-ETB logic in on_resolve). create_token same ordering. Replacement effects only consulted when leaving battlefield AND replacement_event supplied. move_zone deletes stale colors_spent on any zone change.\n   - _resolve_spell: runs card.on_resolve while card is on STACK, then permanents → battlefield via move_to_zone; non-permanents → `Zone.EXILE if getattr(card,\"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\",False) else Zone.GRAVEYARD` (this flag branch is CONFIRMED present in casting.py).\n   - cast_spell: timing+can_cast+hand check → hand→stack → choose targets → mana payment (rollback to hand on fail) → sets `card.colors_spent = list(last_payment_colors)` and `card.mana_spent = pool_total_before - after` → on_cast → push StackObject → fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent. cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone): no timing/mana; finds card in any player's from_zone; rollback to source on target failure; sets `card.mana_spent = 0`; fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent.\n   - copy_spell(game, original_stackobj, controller, new_targets=None) (stack.py): shallow-copies original.source, sets controller/owner, binds on_resolve to copied_card.on_resolve (NO zone movement); returns StackObject — caller must `game.stack.push(copy)`.\n   - _counter_spell pattern (fdn_153): remove StackObject from `game.stack._items` (by identity), remove card from controller's Zone.STACK, add card to owner's Zone.GRAVEYARD.\n   - Continuous effects (continuous_effects.py): ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer=None, apply:(game)->None, timestamp=0, duration=DURATION_PERMANENT). Layer.TYPE=4, ABILITY=6, POWER_TOUGHNESS=7; SubLayer.SET_PT=\"7b\", MODIFY_PT=\"7c\"; DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. game.effect_manager.add(effect) auto-assigns timestamp. apply_all resets battlefield via _reset_characteristics (CardImpl resets card_types→_original_card_types and keywords→_original_keywords; Creature also resets modified_power/toughness→base, counters→_base_*, and _cant_* flags; subtypes NOT reset) then applies sorted by (layer, sublayer-order, timestamp). Modify P/T via obj.modified_power += N. apply_all iterates ONLY battlefield. remove_expired sweeps EOT effects (called in cleanup, then apply_all).\n   - Mana (mana.py): ManaPool.add(ManaType,n), can_pay(cost), pay(cost[,choices]) sets last_payment_colors (distinct Colors via _MANA_TO_COLOR, colorless excluded, sorted by Color.value), get(ManaType)->int, total(), empty(). ManaCost.cmc treats X as 0, hybrid +1 each. ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{U}{U}\"); ManaCost() is empty. No gain_life helper — use player.life += x.\n   - DeterministicPlayer (player.py) pops scripted answers (deque.popleft) for choose_target/choose/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order; ScriptExhaustedError when empty. ALWAYS guard player choices in card code with try/except (ScriptExhaustedError, NotImplementedError).\n   - ZoneContainer (zones.py): index 0 = bottom, -1 = top. add(obj, position=\"top\"), remove(obj) (identity), contains, get_all() (bottom→top copy), top(n) (last n), bottom(n). Library top = last element. draw_card pulls library.top(1)[0].\n   - game.py helpers: deal_damage(game, source, target, amount) (player→life-=, creature→damage_marked+=, fires triggers, handles deathtouch/lifelink/protection); destroy; sacrifice(game, player, perm); exile(game, obj) (finds zone, moves to EXILE); draw_card(game, player) (returns card or None, increments cards_drawn_this_turn, fires DrawsCard); discard(game, player, card) (HAND→GRAVEYARD); create_token(game, player, token) (sets is_token/owner/controller, adds to bf, fires ETB then register_triggers); add_counter/remove_counter; tap/untap.\n   - test_utils.py: create_game(deck1, deck2, scripts=(s1,s2)); set_board_state(game, idx, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana={ManaType:n}) sets owner/controller; cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=) scripts targets via player._script.appendleft reversed, casts, auto-resolves via _resolve_top_of_stack (pop+on_resolve each); declare_attackers(game, names) scripts active._script.appendleft(attackers_list); declare_blockers(game, {atk:[blk]}) scripts defending._script.appendleft(block_map); advance_to_phase(game, phase, step).\n   - combat.py declare_attackers_step: eligible = `[c for c in bf.get_all() if hasattr(c,\"base_power\") and _can_attack(c)]` — CRITICAL: SOS 257 land must NOT have base_power attribute until animated. VIGILANCE prevents tapping. declare_blockers_step eligible filter also uses `hasattr(c,\"base_power\")`.\n   - protection.py reads obj.colors (list of single-letter strings); set self.colors after super().__init__ (sos_stubs pattern, e.g. self.colors=['W'], self.colors=['B','G']).\n   - game_state.py: extra_turns (FIFO seat indices); skip_turns dict[int,int] keyed by seat (decremented/honored in _next_active_player_index). game.players.index(player) gives seat. non_active_player property.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_{1,4,13,57,97,120,201,226,245,257}/card_impl.py` — ALL still `class X(CardImpl): pass`. Class names that MUST be preserved: TheDawningArchaic (sos_1), TogetherAsOne (sos_4), EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares (sos_13), ManaSculpt (sos_57), RalZarekGuestLecturer (sos_97), ImprovisationCapstone (sos_120), LoreholdTheHistorian (sos_201), SilverquillTheDisputant (sos_226), WitherbloomTheBalancer (sos_245), GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex (sos_257).\n   - card_spec.json oracle texts CONFIRMED this session:\n     - sos_245 Witherbloom: \"Affinity for creatures... Flying, deathtouch. Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n     - sos_226 Silverquill: \"Flying, vigilance. Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1.\"\n     - sos_4 Together as One: \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\"\n     - sos_57 Mana Sculpt: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n     - sos_1 Dawning Archaic: \"Costs {1} less per instant/sorcery card in your graveyard. Reach. Whenever ~ attacks, you may cast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n     - sos_13 Emeritus: \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\"\n     - sos_97 Ral Zarek: \"+1: Surveil 2. −1: Any number of target players each discard a card. −2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is the number of coins that came up heads.\"\n     - sos_120 Improvisation Capstone: \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana costs. Paradigm (...cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\"\n     - sos_201 Lorehold: \"Flying, haste. Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\"\n     - sos_257 Great Hall: \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell. {5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n   - `/workspace/cards/stubs/sos_stubs.py` — exact constructors CONFIRMED: TheDawningArchaic(Creature, {10}, {'Avatar'}, LEGENDARY, 7/7, NO colors); TogetherAsOne(Sorcery, {6}, NO colors); EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature, {1}{W}{W}, {'Cat','Cleric'}, 3/3, NOT legendary, colors=['W']); ManaSculpt(Instant, {1}{U}{U}, colors=['U']); RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker, {1}{B}{B}, {'Ral'}, LEGENDARY, starting_loyalty=3, colors=['B']); ImprovisationCapstone(Sorcery, {5}{R}{R}, {'Lesson'}, colors=['R']); LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature, {3}{R}{W}, {'Elder','Dragon'}, LEGENDARY, 5/5, colors=['R','W']); SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature, {2}{W}{B}, {'Elder','Dragon'}, LEGENDARY, 4/4, colors=['B','W']); WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature, {6}{B}{G}, {'Elder','Dragon'}, LEGENDARY, 5/5, colors=['B','G']); GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land, name 'Great Hall of the Biblioplex', ManaCost(), NO colors).\n   - Engine files READ this session (all prior edits CONFIRMED intact, additive-only): card.py (full), continuous_effects.py (full), casting.py (full — _exile flag + static_cost_reduction summing confirmed), stack.py (full — copy_spell at line 72), types.py (full — TargetRequirement at 239), game.py:100-479, abilities.py:180-273, basic_lands.py:40-129, player.py (full), mana.py (full), zones.py (full — move_to_zone), test_utils.py (full), combat.py:200-340, plus game_state.py/turn.py/events.py/triggers.py (re-supplied via reminders).\n   - FDN reference cards READ this session: fdn_272 (Plains ManaAbility), fdn_267 (SecludedCourtyard two ManaAbilities + ENGINE LIMITATION comment for restricted mana), fdn_153 (EssenceScatter — defines `_get_chosen_target` and `_counter_spell` helpers; can_cast scans game.stack.objects() excluding self; get_targets TargetRequirement zone=Zone.STACK), fdn_6 (ClawsOut — cost_reduction affinity + on_resolve adds POWER_TOUGHNESS/MODIFY_PT EOT ContinuousEffect via modified_power+=2), fdn_205 (WardensOfTheCycle — `self.colors_spent:int=0`; on_resolve `count=self.colors_spent` then create_token loop), fdn_44 (KaitoCunningInfiltrator — register_triggers via TriggerRegistration; get_loyalty_abilities returns LoyaltyAbility list reading getattr(pw,'_resolve_target',None); emblem via `type('Emblem',(),{'name':...})()`), fdn_157 (LightshellDuo — surveil 2: `top_cards=cards[-min(2,len(cards)):]; for card in reversed(top_cards): choose_yes_no → library.remove + graveyard.add`), fdn_95 (SowerOfChaos — get_activated_abilities returns ActivatedAbility(cost=_cost(game,src) which pays mana via controller.mana_pool, effect=_effect(game) reads source._current_target)).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors this session (entirely read-only verification). Standing fix carried forward: `python` binary unavailable — always use `python3` or `/usr/local/bin/pytest`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed ManaAbility contract for SOS 257: use side-effect `mana_produced(game)->None` + `cost(game)->bool` (Plains form, source via closure) — and that the engine never auto-invokes them, so tests call directly.\n   - Confirmed combat eligibility uses `hasattr(c,\"base_power\")`, so SOS 257 land must add base_power only on animation (otherwise an un-animated land would be attack-eligible).\n   - Resolved card.py-vs-continuous_effects.py ContinuousEffect name clash: always use engine.continuous_effects.ContinuousEffect.\n   - Converge X handling: handle both int (test) and list (real cast) via `cs if isinstance(cs,int) else len(cs)` (because cast_spell sets colors_spent as a LIST but tests/WardensOfTheCycle treat it as int).\n   - Confirmed SpellCastTriggeredEvent fires AFTER push and copy_spell does NOT fire it (no infinite casualty loop).\n   - One OPEN verification item: where `cards_drawn_this_turn` is RESET each turn (needed for Lorehold miracle `cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`). The last grep only found it incremented in game.py:324-326 and never explicitly found the reset location.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - System reminders re-supplying prior Read results for game_state.py, turn.py, events.py, triggers.py, plus the deferred-tools/ToolSearch note (these opened the session).\n   - \"Continue the conversation from where it left off... Pick up the last task as if the break never happened. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary...\"\n   - Recurring task-list reminders (Tasks #1–#13; #13 completed, #1 in_progress, #2–#12 pending) and \"task tools haven't been used recently\" gentle reminders.\n   - Final CRITICAL instruction: \"Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n   - Preserved constraints (verbatim, still in effect): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\" Additive-only engine rule: \"You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions... You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/`.\" Max 30 tests per card. Card class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Task #1 (in_progress): broader engine wiring — VERIFIED complete this session (SpellCastTriggeredEvent w/ spell/card/controller fired after push, AttacksTriggeredEvent fired, MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent(player=active) fired both mains, EndStepTriggeredEvent fired, BeginningOfUpkeep fired, DrawsCard fired post-increment, static_cost_reduction summed in get_cost_reduction, skip_turns honored, _exile_instead_of_graveyard in _resolve_spell). Can be marked completed.\n   - Tasks #2–#11: Implement the 10 SOS cards (all still stubs).\n   - Task #12: Write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (≤30 each) and run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ cards/ -q` (baseline 1145 passed must hold).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I completed an exhaustive read-only API verification pass (all engine modules + needed FDN reference cards + all 10 SOS specs/stubs/constructors) and finalized complete implementation drafts (in reasoning, NOT yet written to files) for every card. The last tool action was a grep for `cards_drawn_this_turn|_resolve_target|clear_loyalty_tracking|_loyalty_activated_this_turn` which returned: abilities.py:99-122 (clear_loyalty_tracking, _loyalty_activated_this_turn set keyed by (object_id, turn_number)) and game.py:324-326 (cards_drawn_this_turn incremented in draw_card). I had NOT yet confirmed where cards_drawn_this_turn is reset per turn.\n   Finalized per-card implementation plans (ready to write):\n   - SOS 245 WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature {6}{B}{G}, LEGENDARY {'Elder','Dragon'}, 5/5, Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.DEATHTOUCH, colors=['B','G']): helper _creature_count(game,controller) counts CardType.CREATURE on controller's battlefield; cost_reduction → creature count; static_cost_reduction(game,spell,controller) → if self.controller is controller and spell is INSTANT or SORCERY, return creature count, else 0.\n   - SOS 226 SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature {2}{W}{B}, LEGENDARY {'Elder','Dragon'}, 4/4, FLYING|VIGILANCE, colors=['B','W']): register_triggers SpellCastTriggeredEvent, cond=(event.controller is self.controller and event.card is not self and event.card is instant/sorcery); effect(game,event) [2-arg, wrapped]: list creatures power≥1, guarded choose_yes_no, guarded choose creature, sacrifice(game,controller,chosen), copy=copy_spell(game,event.spell,controller), game.stack.push(copy).\n   - SOS 4 TogetherAsOne(Sorcery {6}, NO colors; __init__ sets self.colors_spent=0): get_targets [TargetRequirement(filter hasattr life → target player), TargetRequirement(filter hasattr life/damage_marked/loyalty → any target)]; on_resolve x=converge (cs int-or-len), target_player draws x via draw_card loop, deal_damage(self, damage_target, x), controller.life += x.\n   - SOS 57 ManaSculpt(Instant {1}{U}{U}, colors=['U']): define _get_chosen_target/_counter_spell (fdn_153); can_cast/get_targets target any spell on stack except self (filter `getattr(o,\"source\",None) is not self`); on_resolve: amount=getattr(countered_card,\"mana_spent\",0); _counter_spell; if controller controls a 'Wizard' subtype permanent and amount>0, _setup_delayed_mana → register sentinel-source MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent trigger (cond not-fired and event.player is controller) that adds amount {C} colorless then unregisters sentinel.\n   - SOS 1 TheDawningArchaic(Creature {10}, LEGENDARY {'Avatar'}, 7/7, Keyword.REACH, NO colors): cost_reduction → count instant/sorcery cards in controller graveyard; register_triggers AttacksTriggeredEvent (cond event.creature is self); effect: guarded choose_yes_no, guarded choose among instant/sorcery in graveyard, set chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard=True, cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD) in try/except.\n   - SOS 13 EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature {1}{W}{W}, {'Cat','Cleric'}, 3/3, colors=['W'], self.is_prepared=False): get_targets [target player]; on_resolve creates 1/1 Inkling token (Keyword.FLYING, colors=['W','B']) for target player, then if opp_creature_count > (my_battlefield_creature_count + 1) set is_prepared=True; cast_prepared(game, target_creature) pays {W} best-effort, _swords_to_plowshares (exile target, its controller.life += target.power), is_prepared=False.\n   - SOS 97 RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker {1}{B}{B}, LEGENDARY {'Ral'}, starting_loyalty=3, colors=['B']): get_loyalty_abilities → +1 Surveil 2 (fdn_157), −1 reads pw._resolve_targets (list, fallback to [_resolve_target]) each player guarded-discards (default last card), −2 reads pw._resolve_target creature card MV≤3 in controller graveyard → move_to_zone GRAVEYARD→BATTLEFIELD, −7 flip 5 coins (random.random()<0.5, or `pw._forced_heads` override for deterministic tests) → target opponent (pw._resolve_target or non_active_player) seat += heads in game.skip_turns.\n   - SOS 120 ImprovisationCapstone(Sorcery {5}{R}{R}, {'Lesson'}, colors=['R'], self._is_paradigm_copy=False): _run_dig exiles top of library until total cmc≥4, then guarded free-cast (choose_yes_no per non-land exiled card) via cast_spell_free(...,Zone.EXILE); on_resolve runs dig, and if not _is_paradigm_copy sets self._exile_instead_of_graveyard=True + _setup_paradigm (source=self) registering MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent trigger (cond event.player is controller and game.phase==PRECOMBAT_MAIN and src in controller EXILE) offering paradigm copy → new ImprovisationCapstone(_is_paradigm_copy=True) running _run_dig only.\n   - SOS 201 LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature {3}{R}{W}, LEGENDARY {'Elder','Dragon'}, 5/5, Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE, colors=['R','W']): register_triggers (a) BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent cond game.active_player is not controller → effect guarded choose_yes_no