{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Verbatim task (from prompt.md, still in effect): \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   Also required: write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (≤30 tests each) and run the full suite (`python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ cards/ -q` or `/usr/local/bin/pytest`; `python` is NOT available — use `python3`). Baseline: `pytest engine_tests/ -q` → 1145 passed.\n   Engine modifications MUST be additive-only: \"You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions... You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/`.\" Card class names are predetermined and MUST remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`.\n   Final user instruction: respond with TEXT ONLY, no tool calls, producing this analysis+summary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pure-Python (stdlib only) MTG engine; flat imports from /workspace. `python3` only (no `python`).\n   - CardImpl hooks: can_cast(game)->bool; cost_reduction(game)->int (generic-only self-reduction, clamped to generic≥0); static_cost_reduction(game, spell, controller)->int (summed across ALL battlefield permanents in get_cost_reduction at casting.py:108-117, skipping `perm is card`; `controller` arg = the casting player); on_cast(game); on_resolve(game) (targets via self.chosen_targets set by _resolve_spell while card is on STACK); get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]; register_triggers(game); register_replacement_effects(game); get_activated_abilities()->list[ActivatedAbility]; get_modes(). Planeswalker adds get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]. Land.can_cast→False, get_mana_abilities()->[].\n   - Creature: base_power/base_toughness, modified_power/modified_toughness (reset to base each apply cycle), power/toughness properties (= modified + plus_one_counters − minus_one_counters), summoning_sick default True, damage_marked, is_attacking/is_blocking, plus_one_counters/minus_one_counters, _base_plus_one_counters/_base_minus_one_counters, is_token, dealt_deathtouch_damage. Constructor always adds CardType.CREATURE. _reset_characteristics resets modified P/T→base, counters→_base_*, _cant_* flags, protections.\n   - card.py dataclasses: ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description); LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description); ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description); Mode(name, description). card.py ALSO defines a DIFFERENT ContinuousEffect(apply, remove, description) — DO NOT use; use engine.continuous_effects.ContinuousEffect.\n   - Keyword is enum.Flag (combinable via `|`): FLYING, FIRST_STRIKE, DOUBLE_STRIKE, DEATHTOUCH, TRAMPLE, LIFELINK, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE, FLASH, DEFENDER, HEXPROOF, INDESTRUCTIBLE, MENACE, WARD, PROWESS. Keyword(0) = none.\n   - CardType: CREATURE, INSTANT, SORCERY, ENCHANTMENT, ARTIFACT, PLANESWALKER, LAND. ManaType: WHITE/BLUE/BLACK/RED/GREEN/COLORLESS. ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{U}{U}\"); ManaCost() empty; .cmc treats X as 0, hybrid +1 each; .generic. TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone) — zone is a placeholder for DeterministicPlayer (it just pops scripted answers).\n   - protection.py reads obj.colors (list of single-letter strings). Set self.colors AFTER super().__init__ (sos_stubs already do this for colored cards, e.g. self.colors=['U']).\n   - cast_spell pipeline (casting.py:138): timing→can_cast→hand check→hand→stack→`del card.colors_spent`→choose targets (validate filter_fn, rollback to hand on fail; protection check)→set card.controller if None→get_cost_reduction→pay→`card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` and `card.mana_spent = pool_total_before − after`→on_cast→push StackObject→fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player, card, controller). cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone): no timing/mana; finds card in any player's from_zone; rollback to source on failure; sets `card.mana_spent = 0`; fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent. copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None) shallow-copies source, binds copied_card.chosen_targets+on_resolve, returns StackObject — caller MUST push.\n   - _resolve_spell (casting.py:416): sets card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets; runs on_resolve while card on STACK; permanents → battlefield via move_to_zone; non-permanents → `Zone.EXILE if getattr(card,\"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\",False) else Zone.GRAVEYARD` (CONFIRMED at lines 452-457).\n   - mana.py ManaPool: add(ManaType,n), can_pay(cost), pay(cost[,choices]) (auto-pays generic colorless-first then colored in enum order; records last_payment_colors = sorted distinct Colors of mana actually spent, colorless excluded), total(), get(mt), empty(). No gain_life helper — use player.life += x.\n   - Triggers: TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition:(game,event)->bool|None, effect, source, controller). fire_event matches isinstance (subclass-aware), APNAP order (active player first/bottom). fire_event WRAPS effects accepting ≥2 positional params to call effect(game, event); 1-arg → effect(game). unregister(source) identity-based, auto-called ONLY when leaving battlefield in move_to_zone (triggers with sentinel/graveyard/exile sources PERSIST).\n   - Events: SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=StackObject, player, card, controller) fired after push in cast_spell AND cast_spell_free; copy_spell does NOT fire it. AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker) per attacker. BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (NO fields — use game.active_player). MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player) fired BOTH mains. DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card) fired AFTER incrementing cards_drawn_this_turn. EntersBattlefield, CreatureDies, DealsDamage(source,target,amount,is_combat,combat), LosesLife, GainsLife.\n   - move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None): replacement effects consulted only when leaving battlefield AND replacement_event supplied. Entering battlefield: fires ETB event BEFORE register_triggers (own ETB won't self-fire → put own-ETB in on_resolve, per fdn_2 pattern). Leaving battlefield: fires LeavesBattlefield + CreatureDies (if dest=graveyard) BEFORE unregister. move_zone deletes stale colors_spent.\n   - game.py helpers: deal_damage(game,source,target,amount) (player→life-=, creature→damage_marked+=, protection check, deathtouch/lifelink); sacrifice(game,player,perm); exile(game,obj) (finds zone→EXILE); draw_card(game,player) (returns card/None, increments cards_drawn_this_turn, fires DrawsCard); discard(game,player,card) (HAND→GRAVEYARD); create_token(game,player,token) (sets is_token/owner/controller, adds to bf, fires ETB then register_triggers); add_counter/remove_counter (handles \"+1/+1\",\"-1/-1\",\"loyalty\"); tap/untap.\n   - **CRITICAL FINDING:** `cards_drawn_this_turn` is incremented in game.py:324-326 but NEVER reset by the engine (cumulative). For \"first card each turn\" mechanics (Lorehold miracle), must track a per-turn counter on the card keyed on turn_number (fdn_37 pattern), NOT rely on cards_drawn_this_turn==1.\n   - abilities.py: _activate_loyalty_ability requires is_sorcery_speed + once-per-turn (`_loyalty_activated_this_turn` set keyed by (object_id, turn_number)), pays loyalty (AbilityError if new_loyalty<0), pushes StackObject(on_resolve=ability.effect). clear_loyalty_tracking() clears the set. For TESTS: get_loyalty_abilities returns LoyaltyAbility dataclasses — call `.effect(game)` directly after setting pw._resolve_target / pw._resolve_targets.\n   - DeterministicPlayer (player.py): pops scripted answers (deque.popleft) for choose_target/choose/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order; raises ScriptExhaustedError when empty. ALWAYS guard player choices with try/except (ScriptExhaustedError, NotImplementedError).\n   - game_state.py: extra_turns (FIFO seat indices); skip_turns dict[int,int] keyed by seat (decremented/honored in _next_active_player_index). game.players.index(player)→seat. non_active_player property.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py` (WRITTEN, COMPLETE): WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature) — {6}{B}{G}, LEGENDARY {Elder,Dragon}, 5/5, FLYING|DEATHTOUCH, colors=['B','G']. Module helper `_creature_count(game, controller)` counts CardType.CREATURE on controller's bf. `cost_reduction` returns _creature_count(game, self.controller); `static_cost_reduction(game, spell, controller)` returns _creature_count if self.controller is controller and spell is INSTANT/SORCERY else 0.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py` (WRITTEN, COMPLETE): SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature) — {2}{W}{B}, LEGENDARY {Elder,Dragon}, 4/4, FLYING|VIGILANCE, colors=['B','W']. register_triggers registers SpellCastTriggeredEvent; condition: event.controller is self.controller and event.card is not self and card is INSTANT/SORCERY; effect(g, event) [2-arg]: candidates = controller's creatures power≥1; guarded choose_yes_no, guarded choose_card; sacrifice(g, controller, chosen); copy=copy_spell(g, event.spell, controller); g.stack.push(copy).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` (WRITTEN, COMPLETE): TogetherAsOne(Sorcery) — {6}, no colors; __init__ sets self.colors_spent=0. Module helpers _is_player (hasattr life and zones), _is_any_target (player or hasattr damage_marked/loyalty). get_targets returns [target player, any target]. _converge_x() returns cs if int else len(cs). on_resolve: x=_converge_x; targets[0] draws x via draw_card loop; deal_damage(self, targets[1], x); controller.life += x.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` (WRITTEN, COMPLETE): ManaSculpt(Instant) — {1}{U}{U}, colors=['U']. Defines _get_chosen_target, _counter_spell (fdn_153 copy), _controls_wizard. can_cast/get_targets target any stack object whose source is not self and has card_types. on_resolve: amount=int(getattr(countered_card,\"mana_spent\",0)); _counter_spell; if amount>0 and _controls_wizard → _setup_delayed_mana registers a sentinel-source MainPhaseBeganTriggeredEvent trigger (cond: not fired and event.player is controller) that adds amount COLORLESS to controller.mana_pool then unregisters sentinel (state dict {\"fired\":False}).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` (WRITTEN, COMPLETE): TheDawningArchaic(Creature) — {10}, LEGENDARY {Avatar}, 7/7, REACH, no colors. Helper _instants_sorceries_in_graveyard(game, player). cost_reduction = len of that. register_triggers: AttacksTriggeredEvent cond event.creature/attacker is source; effect: guarded choose_yes_no, guarded choose_card from graveyard instants/sorceries, set chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard=True, cast_spell_free(g, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD) in try/except CastingError.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` (WRITTEN, COMPLETE): EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature) — {1}{W}{W}, {Cat,Cleric}, 3/3, colors=['W'], self.is_prepared=False. get_targets [target player]. on_resolve (own-ETB): create 1/1 Inkling token (keywords=FLYING, colors=['W','B']) for target player (default controller); my_creatures = _creature_count(controller)+1 (Emeritus still on stack); if any opponent's count > my_creatures → is_prepared=True. cast_prepared(game, target_creature): if is_prepared and can_pay {W}, pay, exile target, victim_controller.life += target.power, is_prepared=False, return True.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` (WRITTEN, COMPLETE): RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker) — {1}{B}{B}, LEGENDARY {Ral}, starting_loyalty=3, colors=['B']. get_loyalty_abilities returns 4: +1 _plus1 surveil 2 (fdn_157 pattern, guarded); −1 _minus1 reads pw._resolve_targets (fallback [pw._resolve_target]) each player guarded-discards (default last); −2 _minus2 reads pw._resolve_target creature in controller graveyard with cmc≤3, sets target.controller=controller, move_to_zone GRAVEYARD→BATTLEFIELD; −7 _minus7 heads = int(pw._forced_heads) if set else sum(5 coin flips random.random()<0.5), target = pw._resolve_target (player) or first opponent, game.skip_turns[seat]+=heads.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` (WRITTEN, COMPLETE — most recent): LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature) — {3}{R}{W}, LEGENDARY {Elder,Dragon}, 5/5, FLYING|HASTE, colors=['R','W']. register_triggers registers TWO triggers: (a) DrawsCardTriggeredEvent miracle — condition tracks per-turn first draw via source._miracle_turn/_miracle_draws keyed on g.turn_number, returns True only when controller's draw count==1 and card is INSTANT/SORCERY in controller's hand; effect(g,event) [2-arg]: guarded choose_yes_no, if can_pay {2} pay it, cast_spell_free(g, ctrl, card, Zone.HAND) try/except CastingError. (b) BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent — condition g.active_player is not controller; effect(g): guarded choose_yes_no, guarded choose_card discard (default last), discard, draw_card.\n   - `/workspace/cards/stubs/sos_stubs.py` (READ, confirmed constructors): exact kwargs for all 10 target classes. Key ones: GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land, name 'Great Hall of the Biblioplex', ManaCost(), NO colors); ImprovisationCapstone(Sorcery, {5}{R}{R}, {'Lesson'}, colors=['R']).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_spec.json` (READ): oracle \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared. (While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.)\" Back face Swords to Plowshares {W}.\n   - Engine files READ this session (all confirmed intact, additive-only): casting.py (get_cost_reduction:89, cast_spell:138, cast_spell_free:281, _resolve_spell:416 with _exile flag), card.py (full), types.py (full), player.py (full), game.py:100-479, mana.py (full), stack.py (full, copy_spell:72), zones.py (full, move_to_zone:179), abilities.py (full), plus game_state.py/turn.py/events.py/triggers.py (via reminders).\n   - FDN references READ: fdn_37 (per-turn draw counter), fdn_6 (affinity cost_reduction + EOT P/T buff), fdn_153 (_get_chosen_target/_counter_spell), fdn_44 (loyalty abilities reading pw._resolve_target, emblem via type('Emblem',(),{...})()), fdn_157 (surveil 2: top_cards=cards[-min(2,len):], reversed, choose_yes_no→library.remove+graveyard.add), fdn_2 (own-ETB in on_resolve).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Write to sos_226 initially failed: \"File has not been read yet. Read it first before writing to it.\" Fixed by Reading sos_226/card_impl.py first, then Writing. (All subsequent card files were Read before Write, or were re-Read templates.)\n   - Standing constraint carried forward: `python` binary unavailable — always use `python3` or `/usr/local/bin/pytest`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed `cards_drawn_this_turn` is cumulative (never reset) → Lorehold miracle uses self-tracked per-turn counter (fdn_37 pattern) keyed on turn_number, firing when count==1.\n   - Confirmed static_cost_reduction(game, spell, controller) summing in get_cost_reduction (skips perm is card) → used for Witherbloom granting affinity to controller's instants/sorceries.\n   - Resolved own-ETB ordering: ETB event fires before register_triggers, so Emeritus handles its ETB in on_resolve (fdn_2 pattern); counted Emeritus as +1 since it's still on the stack during on_resolve.\n   - Converge: handle both int (tests set card.colors_spent=N) and list (cast_spell sets list) via `cs if isinstance(cs,int) else len(cs)`.\n   - Mana Sculpt delayed mana: used a sentinel source object so the trigger persists (not unregistered when Mana Sculpt goes to graveyard) and self-unregisters after firing once.\n   - The Dawning Archaic free-cast exile: set chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard=True before cast_spell_free so _resolve_spell sends it to EXILE.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - System reminders re-supplying game_state.py, turn.py, events.py, triggers.py contents, plus the note that casting.py was read but too large, and the deferred-tools/ToolSearch note (opened the session).\n   - \"Continue the conversation from where it left off... Pick up the last task as if the break never happened. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary...\"\n   - Recurring task-list reminders (Tasks #1–#13) and gentle \"task tools haven't been used recently\" reminders.\n   - Final CRITICAL instruction: \"Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n   - Preserved constraints (verbatim, still in effect): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\" Additive-only engine rule: \"You may add new methods, classes