pstone(_is_paradigm_copy=True) running _run_dig only.\n   - SOS 257 GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land, ManaCost(), NO colors): get_mana_abilities → [{T}:Add {C} (cost taps, mana_produced side-effect adds COLORLESS), {T}+Pay 1 life:Add chosen color (restriction \"only for instant/sorcery\" is ENGINE LIMITATION/unenforced)]; get_activated_abilities → [{5} animate: cost pays {5}; effect if not _is_animated → set _is_animated=True, set base_power=2/base_toughness=4 + creature attrs (modified_power/toughness, damage_marked, summoning flags, counters, _base_* counters), add 'Wizard' subtype + CREATURE card_type, add permanent TYPE-layer ContinuousEffect re-adding {CREATURE}+'Wizard', register SpellCastTriggeredEvent +1/+0 EOT pump for controller's instant/sorcery]; override _reset_characteristics to reset modified P/T→base ONLY when _is_animated; define defensive power/toughness via getattr; do NOT define base_power until animated (combat eligibility uses hasattr(c,\"base_power\") in combat.py declare_attackers_step/declare_blockers_step).\n   ManaAbility contract (basic_lands.py/fdn_267): cost is a callable that PAYS and returns bool (Plains form `cost(game)->bool` via closure, or fdn_267 form `cost(game, src)->bool`); mana_produced is a side-effect `(game)->None` adding mana to controller's pool. Engine NEVER auto-invokes ManaAbility — tests must call them directly.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue implementing the remaining cards, directly in line with the task \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257\". Concretely: (a) mark Task #8 (Lorehold) completed; (b) Read then Write `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py` (ImprovisationCapstone) and `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py` (GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex) per the finalized plans above (changing base class CardImpl→Sorcery/Land); (c) write ≤30 tests per card at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (using `from test_utils import create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell`, `from cards.sos.sos_<N>.card_impl import <Class>`, setting card.colors_spent/card.mana_spent/pw._resolve_target/pw._forced_heads directly and calling on_resolve(game)/loyalty effect(game)/ability cost(game,src)+effect(game)); (d) run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ cards/ -q` and confirm the 1145-test baseline still passes plus the new tests. Before writing sos_257, Read /workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_272 or basic_lands.py and fdn_267 to re-confirm the exact ManaAbility cost/mana_produced calling convention and continuous_effects.ContinuousEffect signature (Layer.TYPE=4, Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS=7, SubLayer.MODIFY_PT=\"7c\", DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/f8a3aed6-12f8-4341-9631-2336f98abe5d.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8a3aed6-12f8-4341-9631-2336f98abe5d","uuid":"a5b81aef-1a39-49d6-8ff4-c72d8ad3f8e7","timestamp":"2026-06-04T06:49:41.391Z","isSynthetic":true}
