y), no tool calls.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pure-Python (stdlib only) MTG engine; flat imports from /workspace. `python3` only.\n   - **test_utils.py is at `/workspace/test_utils.py`** (NOT /workspace/cards/test_utils.py). conftest.py inserts /workspace on sys.path. Tests import `from test_utils import create_game, set_board_state, _resolve_top_of_stack` and `from cards.sos.sos_<N>.card_impl import <Class>`.\n   - test_utils.create_game(deck1=None, deck2=None, *, player1_life=20, player2_life=20, scripts=(script1, script2)) → GameState with two DeterministicPlayer (game.players[0/1]). set_board_state(game, player_index, *, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana={ManaType:int}) replaces zone contents and sets owner/controller. Does NOT set library — add library cards manually via `player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY].add(c)` (top of library = last added). _resolve_top_of_stack(game) loops popping the stack and calling obj.on_resolve(game)+resolve_state_based_actions until empty.\n   - DeterministicPlayer (player.py): ALL of choose_target/choose/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order pop from a single `_script` deque (popleft); ScriptExhaustedError when empty. Card impls guard choices with try/except (ScriptExhaustedError, NotImplementedError).\n   - **CRITICAL (triggers.py): `fire_event` does NOT run effects immediately — it pushes StackObject(on_resolve=...) onto game.stack in APNAP order.** To observe a trigger's effect in a test, fire the event then resolve the stack (`_resolve_top_of_stack(game)` or pop+on_resolve). `_effect_accepts_event` wraps effects with ≥2 positional params to call effect(game, event); 1-arg → effect(game). unregister(source) is identity-based; auto-called only when leaving battlefield. get_triggers_for_source(source) returns list.\n   - Continuous effects (continuous_effects.py): `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer=None, apply=callable(game)->None, timestamp=0, duration=DURATION_PERMANENT)`. Layer IntEnum: COPY=1, CONTROL=2, TEXT=3, TYPE=4, COLOR=5, ABILITY=6, POWER_TOUGHNESS=7. SubLayer: MODIFY_PT=\"7c\" etc. DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. EffectManager.add(effect), apply_all(game) (resets all battlefield objects via _reset_characteristics, then applies effects sorted by layer/sublayer/timestamp), remove_expired(game) sweeps EOT effects. **apply_all/remove_expired are ONLY auto-called at cleanup (turn.py:133-136).** So a card adding an EOT effect must call game.effect_manager.apply_all(game) itself to make it visible immediately.\n   - card.py: CardImpl._reset_characteristics resets card_types→_original_card_types, keywords→_original_keywords (does NOT touch modified_power). Creature._reset_characteristics additionally resets modified_power/toughness→base and counters. Land.can_cast→False, get_mana_abilities()→[]. Creature.power = modified_power + plus_one - minus_one (property). Combat eligibility uses `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")`.\n   - ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description): cost is `(game, src) -> bool` (pays cost), mana_produced is `(game) -> None`. Engine NEVER auto-invokes ManaAbility — tests call directly.\n   - ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description): activate_ability invokes `cost(game, source) -> bool` then mana abilities `effect(game)` immediately / non-mana push StackObject.\n   - LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description): tests call `.effect(game)` directly after setting pw._resolve_target / pw._resolve_targets / pw._forced_heads.\n   - cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone): finds card in any player's from_zone, moves to stack, sets card.mana_spent=0, pushes StackObject, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent. _resolve_spell sends non-permanents to Zone.EXILE if `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard` else GRAVEYARD.\n   - copy_spell(game, original, controller) returns a StackObject; does NOT fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent. Caller must push.\n   - Events (events.py): SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller); AttacksTriggere